window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 27 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072681","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What comes next in the series?<br>1, 1, 4, 9, 25, 64, 169, 441, 1156, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी में आगे क्या आएगा?<br>1, 1, 4, 9, 25, 64, 169, 441, 1156, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2250"},"2":{"en":"3025"},"3":{"en":"1339"},"4":{"en":"3773"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The square roots of the terms are 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21 and 34, which is the Fibonacci series where every number is the sum of the two before it<br>The next Fibonacci number is 34 + 21 = 55<br>So the next term is 55² = 3025<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3025.</b>","hi":"पदों के वर्गमूल 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21 तथा 34 हैं, जो फिबोनाची श्रेणी है जिसमें प्रत्येक संख्या अपने पहले की दो संख्याओं का योग है<br>अगली फिबोनाची संख्या 34 + 21 = 55 है<br>अतः अगला पद 55² = 3025 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3025 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072682","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A person spends 40% of his salary on rent, 25% on food, and saves Rs. 600. If his salary is Rs. 3000, how much does he spend on other expenses? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति अपने वेतन का 40% किराए पर, 25% भोजन पर व्यय करता है और 600 रुपये बचाता है। यदि उसका वेतन 3000 रुपये है, तो वह अन्य व्ययों पर कितना व्यय करता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 200","hi":"200 रुपये"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 450","hi":"450 रुपये"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 300","hi":"300 रुपये"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 600","hi":"600 रुपये"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Rent = 40% of 3000 = 1200 and food = 25% of 3000 = 750<br>Savings = 600, so the total of rent, food and savings is 1200 + 750 + 600 = 2550<br>Other expenses = 3000 − 2550 = 450<br>Hence he spends Rs. 450 on other expenses<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Rs. 450.</b>","hi":"किराया = 3000 का 40% = 1200 तथा भोजन = 3000 का 25% = 750<br>बचत = 600, अतः किराया, भोजन तथा बचत का योग 1200 + 750 + 600 = 2550 है<br>अन्य व्यय = 3000 − 2550 = 450<br>अतः वह अन्य व्ययों पर 450 रुपये व्यय करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 450 रुपये है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072683","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the odd one out based on digital sum:<br>27, 36, 45, 54, 65 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अंक-योग के आधार पर विषम पद चुनिए:<br>27, 36, 45, 54, 65 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"27"},"2":{"en":"54"},"3":{"en":"65"},"4":{"en":"45"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The digital sum is found by adding the digits: 2 + 7 = 9, 3 + 6 = 9, 4 + 5 = 9 and 5 + 4 = 9<br>For 65 the digital sum is 6 + 5 = 11 and then 1 + 1 = 2<br>So 65 is the odd one out<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 65.</b>","hi":"अंकों को जोड़कर अंक-योग निकाला जाता है: 2 + 7 = 9, 3 + 6 = 9, 4 + 5 = 9 तथा 5 + 4 = 9<br>65 का अंक-योग 6 + 5 = 11 और फिर 1 + 1 = 2 है<br>अतः 65 विषम पद है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 65 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072684","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Out of 60 people, 35 read Newspaper A, 30 read Newspaper B, and 15 read both. How many people read only Newspaper B? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"60 लोगों में से 35 अख़बार A पढ़ते हैं, 30 अख़बार B पढ़ते हैं तथा 15 दोनों पढ़ते हैं। कितने लोग केवल अख़बार B पढ़ते हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"25"},"3":{"en":"20"},"4":{"en":"30"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The people who read only B are those who read B but not A<br>That number is 30 − 15 = 15<br>So 15 people read only Newspaper B<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15.</b>","hi":"केवल B पढ़ने वाले वे लोग हैं जो B पढ़ते हैं परंतु A नहीं<br>यह संख्या 30 − 15 = 15 है<br>अतः 15 लोग केवल अख़बार B पढ़ते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072685","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>1, 4, 9, 16, 25, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>1, 4, 9, 16, 25, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35"},"2":{"en":"36"},"3":{"en":"49"},"4":{"en":"40"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The terms are the squares of 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5: 1, 4, 9, 16 and 25<br>So the next term is 6² = 36<br>Hence the next number is 36<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 36.</b>","hi":"पद 1, 2, 3, 4 तथा 5 के वर्ग हैं: 1, 4, 9, 16 तथा 25<br>अतः अगला पद 6² = 36 है<br>इसलिए अगली संख्या 36 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 36 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072686","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"PROJECT\" is written as \"NPMHCAR.\" How will \"ANCIENT\" be written? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"PROJECT\" को \"NPMHCAR\" लिखा जाता है। \"ANCIENT\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"YLACGLR"},"2":{"en":"YLAGCLR"},"3":{"en":"YLGCALR"},"4":{"en":"YLLCGAR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each letter moves two places back: P→N, R→P, O→M, J→H, E→C, C→A, T→R = NPMHCAR<br>ANCIENT: A→Y, N→L, C→A, I→G, E→C, N→L, T→R<br>Code = YLAGCLR<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): YLAGCLR.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर दो स्थान पीछे जाता है: P→N, R→P, O→M, J→H, E→C, C→A, T→R = NPMHCAR<br>ANCIENT: A→Y, N→L, C→A, I→G, E→C, N→L, T→R<br>कोड = YLAGCLR<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): YLAGCLR है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072687","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In this following question, four words have been given, out of which three are alike in some manner and the fourth one is different. Choose odd one out. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में चार शब्द दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं और चौथा भिन्न है। विषम शब्द चुनिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Goa","hi":"गोवा"},"2":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Maharashtra","hi":"महाराष्ट्र"},"4":{"en":"Karnataka","hi":"कर्नाटक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Goa, Maharashtra and Karnataka all lie along the western coast of India and have a sea coast<br>Madhya Pradesh is a landlocked state with no coastline<br>So Madhya Pradesh is the odd one out<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Madhya Pradesh.</b>","hi":"गोवा, महाराष्ट्र तथा कर्नाटक तीनों भारत के पश्चिमी तट पर स्थित हैं और उनकी समुद्री सीमा है<br>मध्य प्रदेश एक स्थलरुद्ध राज्य है जिसकी कोई तटरेखा नहीं है<br>अतः मध्य प्रदेश विषम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मध्य प्रदेश है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072688","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>HOV, JPX, LQZ, NRB, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न जाँचिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>HOV, JPX, LQZ, NRB, ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"POS"},"2":{"en":"PSD"},"3":{"en":"PVS"},"4":{"en":"QUP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The first letters H, J, L, N move two places ahead each time, so the next first letter is P<br>The second letters O, P, Q, R move one place ahead each time, so the next second letter is S<br>The third letters V, X, Z, B move two places ahead each time, so after B the next third letter is D<br>Hence the next set of letters is PSD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): PSD.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर H, J, L, N प्रत्येक बार दो स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर P है<br>दूसरे अक्षर O, P, Q, R प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर S है<br>तीसरे अक्षर V, X, Z, B प्रत्येक बार दो स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः B के बाद अगला तीसरा अक्षर D है<br>इसलिए अगला अक्षर-समूह PSD है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): PSD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072689","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Rahul says, 'Seema's mother is the only daughter of my mother.'<br>How is Rahul related to Seema? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"राहुल कहता है, 'सीमा की माता मेरी माता की एकमात्र पुत्री है।'<br>राहुल का सीमा से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"},"2":{"en":"Maternal Uncle","hi":"मामा"},"3":{"en":"Brother","hi":"भाई"},"4":{"en":"Grandfather","hi":"दादा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"51\" y=\"62\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"154\" y=\"116\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M130 28V50M76 50H183M76 50V62M183 50V62M183 82V104M183 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"130\" y=\"22\">Mother−</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"76\">Rahul+</text><text x=\"183\" y=\"76\">Seema's mother−</text><text x=\"183\" y=\"130\">Seema−</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>Seema's mother is Rahul's only sister, so Rahul is Seema's maternal uncle.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Maternal Uncle.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"51\" y=\"62\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"154\" y=\"116\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M130 28V50M76 50H183M76 50V62M183 50V62M183 82V104M183 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"130\" y=\"22\">Mother−</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"76\">Rahul+</text><text x=\"183\" y=\"76\">Seema's mother−</text><text x=\"183\" y=\"130\">Seema−</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>सीमा की माता राहुल की इकलौती बहन है, अतः राहुल, सीमा का मामा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072690","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न पूरा करने के लिए चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनिए:<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a regular pentagon carrying concentric curves and a small dark dot at its centre, and it is divided into equal triangular parts from the centre<br>The missing part is the lower right part of this pentagon, so it must carry the dark corner at its top and the same set of curved lines inside the trapezium, with no extra straight lines<br>Option A has no dark corner, option B has the dark corner but misses the inner curves and option C shows extra crossing lines<br>Only the figure of option 4 keeps the dark corner and the smooth curves of the original, so the pattern is completed by the fourth alternative<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक सम पंचभुज है जिसमें संकेंद्री वक्र रेखाएँ तथा केंद्र पर छोटा काला बिंदु है, और यह केंद्र से बराबर त्रिभुजाकार भागों में विभाजित है<br>लुप्त भाग इस पंचभुज का निचला दायाँ भाग है, अतः उसमें ऊपर काला कोना तथा समलंब के भीतर वही वक्र रेखाएँ होनी चाहिए, कोई अतिरिक्त सीधी रेखा नहीं<br>विकल्प A में काला कोना नहीं है, विकल्प B में काला कोना है परंतु भीतरी वक्र रेखाएँ नहीं हैं और विकल्प C में अतिरिक्त काटती रेखाएँ हैं<br>केवल विकल्प 4 की आकृति में काला कोना तथा मूल की चिकनी वक्र रेखाएँ हैं, अतः पैटर्न चौथे विकल्प से पूरा होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q10_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072691","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"From the word 'HEADMASTER', identify which of the given options cannot be formed. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"शब्द 'HEADMASTER' से पहचानिए कि दिए गए विकल्पों में से कौन-सा नहीं बनाया जा सकता। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"STREAM"},"2":{"en":"TEACHER"},"3":{"en":"MASTERED"},"4":{"en":"HAMSTER"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"HEADMASTER has the letters H, E, A, D, M, A, S, T, E, R, so it has two A's, two E's and one each of H, D, M, S, T, R<br>STREAM, MASTERED and HAMSTER can all be made from these letters<br>TEACHER needs the letter C, and there is no C in HEADMASTER<br>So TEACHER cannot be formed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): TEACHER.</b>","hi":"HEADMASTER में अक्षर H, E, A, D, M, A, S, T, E, R हैं, अतः इसमें दो A, दो E तथा H, D, M, S, T, R में से प्रत्येक एक बार है<br>STREAM, MASTERED तथा HAMSTER इन सभी अक्षरों से बन सकते हैं<br>TEACHER के लिए अक्षर C चाहिए, और HEADMASTER में C नहीं है<br>अतः TEACHER नहीं बनाया जा सकता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): TEACHER है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072692","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Which Venn diagram correctly shows the relationship among Cars, Electric Vehicles, and Vehicles? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा वेन आरेख Cars, Electric Vehicles तथा Vehicles के बीच संबंध सही दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"All cars are vehicles and all electric vehicles are vehicles, so both groups lie inside the big circle of vehicles<br>Some cars are electric vehicles, so the two small circles overlap each other<br>Only the first diagram shows two overlapping circles inside one large circle<br>Hence the first diagram is correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"सभी कारें वाहन हैं और सभी इलेक्ट्रिक वाहन भी वाहन हैं, अतः दोनों समूह वाहनों के बड़े वृत्त के भीतर हैं<br>कुछ कारें इलेक्ट्रिक वाहन हैं, अतः दोनों छोटे वृत्त एक-दूसरे को काटते हैं<br>केवल पहला आरेख एक बड़े वृत्त के भीतर दो काटते हुए वृत्त दर्शाता है<br>अतः पहला आरेख सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q12_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072693","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which center code does <b>not</b> maintain the pattern of two digits followed by two letters? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा केंद्र कूट दो अंकों के बाद दो अक्षरों का पैटर्न <b>नहीं</b> रखता? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11AB"},"2":{"en":"22CD"},"3":{"en":"E34F"},"4":{"en":"55GH"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The pattern requires two digits first and then two letters<br>11AB, 22CD and 55GH all begin with two digits and end with two letters<br>E34F begins with a letter and has only one letter at the end, so the pattern is broken<br>Hence E34F does not maintain the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): E34F.</b>","hi":"पैटर्न में पहले दो अंक और फिर दो अक्षर होने चाहिए<br>11AB, 22CD तथा 55GH सभी दो अंकों से शुरू होकर दो अक्षरों पर समाप्त होते हैं<br>E34F अक्षर से शुरू होता है और अंत में केवल एक अक्षर है, अतः पैटर्न टूट जाता है<br>इसलिए E34F पैटर्न नहीं रखता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): E34F है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072694","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"27"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every row the fourth number is the third number multiplied by the second number and divided by the first number<br>First row: 18 × 4 ÷ 6 = 12 ✔ and second row: 16 × 5 ÷ 2 = 40 ✔<br>Third row: 32 × 3 ÷ 8 = 12<br>So the missing number is 12<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 12.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में चौथी संख्या तीसरी संख्या को दूसरी से गुणा करके पहली से भाग देने पर मिलती है<br>पहली पंक्ति: 18 × 4 ÷ 6 = 12 ✔ तथा दूसरी पंक्ति: 16 × 5 ÷ 2 = 40 ✔<br>तीसरी पंक्ति: 32 × 3 ÷ 8 = 12<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 12 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072695","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Which two signs and two numbers need to be interchanged to make the given equation correct?<br>6 × 4 + 12 − 2 ÷ 3 = 6 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए समीकरण को सही बनाने के लिए कौन-से दो चिह्न तथा दो संख्याएँ परस्पर बदलनी होंगी?<br>6 × 4 + 12 − 2 ÷ 3 = 6 [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"× and +, 4 and 2","hi":"× तथा +, 4 तथा 2"},"2":{"en":"+ and −, 6 and 3","hi":"+ तथा −, 6 तथा 3"},"3":{"en":"× and ÷, 4 and 3","hi":"× तथा ÷, 4 तथा 3"},"4":{"en":"+ and ÷, 12 and 3","hi":"+ तथा ÷, 12 तथा 3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Interchanging × with ÷ and 4 with 3 gives 6 ÷ 3 + 12 − 2 × 4<br>6 ÷ 3 = 2 and 2 × 4 = 8, so the value is 2 + 12 − 8 = 6 ✔<br>The other options do not give 6<br>So × and ÷, 4 and 3 must be interchanged<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): × and ÷, 4 and 3.</b>","hi":"× के स्थान पर ÷ तथा 4 के स्थान पर 3 रखने से 6 ÷ 3 + 12 − 2 × 4 बनता है<br>6 ÷ 3 = 2 तथा 2 × 4 = 8, अतः मान 2 + 12 − 8 = 6 है ✔<br>अन्य विकल्प 6 नहीं देते<br>अतः × तथा ÷, 4 तथा 3 परस्पर बदलने होंगे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): × तथा ÷, 4 तथा 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072696","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Science and technology have played a crucial role in improving the standard of living of people across the world.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Science and technology are responsible for all improvements in human life.<br>II. Living standards have improved due to scientific progress. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>विज्ञान और प्रौद्योगिकी ने दुनिया भर के लोगों के जीवन स्तर को सुधारने में महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाई है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. मानव जीवन के सभी सुधारों के लिए विज्ञान और प्रौद्योगिकी उत्तरदायी हैं।<br>II. वैज्ञानिक प्रगति के कारण जीवन स्तर सुधरा है। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The statement says science and technology played a crucial role, which is a major but not the only contribution, so the sweeping word all in conclusion I makes it too broad and it does not follow<br>The direct claim that living standards improved due to scientific progress is exactly what the statement says, so conclusion II follows<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन कहता है कि विज्ञान और प्रौद्योगिकी ने महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाई, जो बड़ा परंतु एकमात्र योगदान नहीं है, अतः निष्कर्ष I में 'सभी' शब्द उसे अत्यधिक व्यापक बना देता है और वह नहीं निकलता<br>यह सीधा कथन कि वैज्ञानिक प्रगति से जीवन स्तर सुधरा, वही है जो कथन कहता है, अतः निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072697","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Those who were genuinely committed to reviving the economy should have strongly supported measures that reduce the spread of infections while allowing businesses to continue operating, especially encouraging the widespread use of face masks.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The Government of America has failed to make people follow the rules on mask-wearing.<br>II. The government of America is only bothered about business and not the citizens. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>जो लोग अर्थव्यवस्था को पुनर्जीवित करने के लिए वास्तव में प्रतिबद्ध थे, उन्हें संक्रमण फैलाव कम करने वाले तथा व्यवसाय जारी रखने देने वाले उपायों का, विशेषकर फेस मास्क के व्यापक प्रयोग को प्रोत्साहित करने वाले उपायों का, दृढ़ता से समर्थन करना चाहिए था।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. अमेरिका सरकार मास्क पहनने के नियमों का पालन कराने में असफल रही है।<br>II. अमेरिका सरकार केवल व्यवसाय की चिंता करती है, नागरिकों की नहीं। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement is a general expectation about people who want the economy revived, and it does not mention America or any government action, so nothing can be concluded about the failure of the American government and inference I does not follow<br>It also never says that any government cares only about business, so inference II does not follow<br>Hence neither inference follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन उन लोगों के बारे में एक सामान्य अपेक्षा है जो अर्थव्यवस्था को पुनर्जीवित करना चाहते हैं, और यह अमेरिका या किसी सरकारी कार्यवाही का उल्लेख नहीं करता, अतः अमेरिकी सरकार की असफलता के बारे में कुछ नहीं निकलता और निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>यह यह भी नहीं कहता कि कोई सरकार केवल व्यवसाय की चिंता करती है, अतः निष्कर्ष II भी नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072698","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line MN, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि रेखा MN पर दर्पण रखा जाए, तो प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब कौन-सी आकृति होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The mirror is on the vertical line MN, so left and right interchange while up and down remain the same<br>Reading from right to left, the mirror image must begin with the flipped 3, then 7, 5, m, y and end with the flipped h<br>Only the first option shows all six characters flipped in their own shapes and in the mirrored order<br>Hence the first option is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण ऊर्ध्व रेखा MN पर है, अतः बायाँ-दायाँ बदल जाता है और ऊपर-नीचे वही रहता है<br>दाएँ से बाएँ पढ़ने पर दर्पण प्रतिबिंब पलटे हुए 3 से शुरू होकर 7, 5, m, y तथा अंत में पलटे हुए h पर समाप्त होना चाहिए<br>केवल पहले विकल्प में सभी छह अक्षर अपने आकार में पलटे हुए तथा दर्पण क्रम में हैं<br>अतः पहला विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072699","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The national literacy rate is increasing, yet the dropout rate in primary schools remains high.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Primary schools are failing to provide adequate infrastructure for children.<br>II. Literacy and primary school retention are not directly proportional in this context. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>राष्ट्रीय साक्षरता दर बढ़ रही है, फिर भी प्राथमिक विद्यालयों में छोड़ने की दर ऊँची बनी हुई है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. प्राथमिक विद्यालय बच्चों के लिए पर्याप्त अवसंरचना उपलब्ध कराने में असफल हैं।<br>II. इस संदर्भ में साक्षरता तथा प्राथमिक विद्यालय में टिकाऊपन सीधे अनुपात में नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The statement puts a rising literacy rate beside a high dropout rate, which shows that the two do not rise and fall together, so conclusion II follows<br>It does not give any reason for the dropouts and says nothing about infrastructure, so conclusion I does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only Conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन बढ़ती साक्षरता दर के साथ ऊँची छोड़ने की दर रखता है, जिससे दिखता है कि दोनों साथ-साथ नहीं बढ़ते, अतः निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>यह छोड़ने का कोई कारण नहीं देता और अवसंरचना के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहता, अतः निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072700","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"PLANTS\" is written as \"PmAoTt\". How will \"STREAM\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"PLANTS\" को \"PmAoTt\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"STREAM\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SuRfBn"},"2":{"en":"SuRfAm"},"3":{"en":"SuRfAn"},"4":{"en":"SuRgAn"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"PLANTS → PmAoTt: letters at odd places stay the same (P, A, T); letters at even places move one step ahead and become small (L→m, N→o, S→t)<br>STREAM: S, T→u, R, E→f, A, M→n<br>Code = SuRfAn<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): SuRfAn.</b>","hi":"PLANTS → PmAoTt: विषम स्थानों के अक्षर वैसे ही रहते हैं (P, A, T); सम स्थानों के अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़कर छोटे हो जाते हैं (L→m, N→o, S→t)<br>STREAM: S, T→u, R, E→f, A, M→n<br>कूट = SuRfAn<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): SuRfAn है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072701","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Select the correct mirror image of the given combination when the mirror is placed at PQ as shown.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिखाए अनुसार जब दर्पण PQ पर रखा जाए, तो दिए गए संयोजन का सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The mirror lies on the vertical line PQ, so the sequence r j 7 3 d k is reversed in order and every character is flipped horizontally while staying at the same height<br>The image must therefore read from the flipped k, then d, 3, 7, j and finally the flipped r<br>Only the first option keeps this exact order with every character properly flipped<br>Hence the first option is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण ऊर्ध्व रेखा PQ पर है, अतः क्रम r j 7 3 d k उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर उसी ऊँचाई पर क्षैतिज रूप से पलटता है<br>अतः प्रतिबिंब पलटे हुए k से शुरू होकर d, 3, 7, j तथा अंत में पलटे हुए r तक पढ़ा जाना चाहिए<br>केवल पहले विकल्प में यही क्रम है और प्रत्येक अक्षर ठीक से पलटा है<br>अतः पहला विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q21_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072702","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Divana is planning a birthday party on 29/03/2026. Her friend Bokul is very introverted and dislikes crowded places. She enjoys reading books, drinking coffee, and having quiet conversations. Divana wants Bokul to attend the party.<br>Which venue should Divana choose? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिवाना 29/03/2026 को जन्मदिन की पार्टी की योजना बना रही है। उसकी मित्र बोकुल बहुत अंतर्मुखी है और भीड़-भाड़ वाले स्थान पसंद नहीं करती। उसे किताबें पढ़ना, कॉफ़ी पीना तथा शांत बातचीत करना पसंद है। दिवाना चाहती है कि बोकुल पार्टी में आए।<br>दिवाना को कौन-सा स्थान चुनना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A large nightclub with loud music and dance performances.","hi":"तीव्र संगीत तथा नृत्य प्रस्तुतियों वाला बड़ा नाइटक्लब।"},"2":{"en":"A peaceful café with a reading corner, coffee, and light snacks.","hi":"पढ़ने का कोना, कॉफ़ी तथा हल्के नाश्ते वाला शांत कैफ़े।"},"3":{"en":"A sports stadium hosting a live match.","hi":"लाइव मैच वाला खेल स्टेडियम।"},"4":{"en":"An amusement park with thrilling rides.","hi":"रोमांचक झूलों वाला मनोरंजन पार्क।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Bokul dislikes crowds and enjoys books, coffee and quiet talk, so the venue must be calm and small<br>A peaceful café with a reading corner, coffee and light snacks matches her interests and keeps the gathering uncrowded<br>The nightclub, the stadium and the amusement park are all loud and crowded and she would be uncomfortable there<br>So the peaceful café is the right venue<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A peaceful café with a reading corner, coffee, and light snacks.</b>","hi":"बोकुल को भीड़ पसंद नहीं है और उसे किताबें, कॉफ़ी तथा शांत बातचीत पसंद है, अतः स्थान शांत और छोटा होना चाहिए<br>पढ़ने के कोने, कॉफ़ी तथा हल्के नाश्ते वाला शांत कैफ़े उसकी रुचि से मेल खाता है और भीड़ भी नहीं होगी<br>नाइटक्लब, स्टेडियम तथा मनोरंजन पार्क सभी शोरगुल व भीड़ भरे हैं और वहाँ वह असहज होगी<br>अतः शांत कैफ़े सही स्थान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): पढ़ने का कोना, कॉफ़ी तथा हल्के नाश्ते वाला शांत कैफ़े। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072703","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given, followed by three conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>No chart is a casket.<br>Not a single casket is a house.<br>Every house is an adapter.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some adapters which are houses are charts as well.<br>II. No chart is a house.<br>III. Some adapters are houses. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद तीन निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कोई चार्ट कैस्केट नहीं है।<br>एक भी कैस्केट घर नहीं है।<br>प्रत्येक घर एडाप्टर है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ एडाप्टर जो घर हैं, चार्ट भी हैं।<br>II. कोई चार्ट घर नहीं है।<br>III. कुछ एडाप्टर घर हैं। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion III follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष III निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions II and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष II और III दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Either conclusion I or conclusion II follows","hi":"या तो निष्कर्ष I या निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"All conclusions follow","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Every house is an adapter and there are houses, so some adapters are certainly houses and conclusion III follows<br>The statements only separate charts from caskets and caskets from houses; a chart may still be a house, so conclusion II cannot be concluded and conclusion I also does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion III follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion III follows.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक घर एडाप्टर है और घर मौजूद हैं, अतः कुछ एडाप्टर निश्चित रूप से घर हैं और निष्कर्ष III निकलता है<br>कथन केवल चार्ट को कैस्केट से तथा कैस्केट को घर से अलग करते हैं; चार्ट फिर भी घर हो सकता है, अतः निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता और निष्कर्ष I भी नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष III निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष III निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072704","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A state government has decided to restore several abandoned lakes to improve groundwater availability in nearby villages. Which assumption underlies this decision? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक राज्य सरकार ने आस-पास के गाँवों में भूजल उपलब्धता सुधारने के लिए कई परित्यक्त झीलों को पुनर्जीवित करने का निर्णय लिया है। इस निर्णय के पीछे कौन-सी अवधारणा निहित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Every restored lake will maintain identical water levels throughout the year regardless of rainfall patterns or climatic variations.","hi":"प्रत्येक पुनर्जीवित झील वर्ष भर वर्षा के प्रारूप या जलवायु परिवर्तन की परवाह किए बिना समान जलस्तर बनाए रखेगी।"},"2":{"en":"Restoring lakes can improve groundwater recharge and increase water availability in nearby villages and communities.","hi":"झीलों को पुनर्जीवित करने से भूजल पुनर्भरण बेहतर हो सकता है और आस-पास के गाँवों तथा समुदायों में जल उपलब्धता बढ़ सकती है।"},"3":{"en":"Residents living near restored lakes will completely stop depending on alternative water sources available within their communities.","hi":"पुनर्जीवित झीलों के निकट रहने वाले निवासी समुदायों में उपलब्ध वैकल्पिक जल स्रोतों पर निर्भरता पूरी तरह बंद कर देंगे।"},"4":{"en":"Groundwater shortages are caused entirely by the absence of lakes rather than by multiple environmental and human factors.","hi":"भूजल की कमी पूरी तरह झीलों की अनुपस्थिति से होती है, कई पर्यावरणीय तथा मानवीय कारकों से नहीं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The decision links restoring lakes with better groundwater availability, which is meaningful only if lakes help recharge groundwater and thus raise water availability in the villages<br>The other options promise identical water levels, total independence from other sources and a single cause for all shortages, all of which are extreme and not needed by the decision<br>So the assumption is that restoring lakes improves groundwater recharge and increases water availability<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Restoring lakes can improve groundwater recharge and increase water availability in nearby villages and communities.</b>","hi":"निर्णय झीलों को पुनर्जीवित करने को भूजल उपलब्धता से जोड़ता है, जो तभी तर्कसंगत है जब झीलें भूजल पुनर्भरण में सहायक हों और इससे गाँवों में जल उपलब्धता बढ़े<br>अन्य विकल्प समान जलस्तर, अन्य स्रोतों से पूर्ण स्वतंत्रता तथा सभी कमियों का एक ही कारण बताते हैं, जो अत्यधिक हैं और निर्णय के लिए आवश्यक नहीं<br>अतः अवधारणा यह है कि झीलों को पुनर्जीवित करने से भूजल पुनर्भरण सुधरता है और जल उपलब्धता बढ़ती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): झीलों को पुनर्जीवित करने से भूजल पुनर्भरण बेहतर हो सकता है और आस-पास के गाँवों तथा समुदायों में जल उपलब्धता बढ़ सकती है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072705","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures which will continue the same series as established by the five Problem Figures.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पाँच समस्या आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाने वाली आकृति उत्तर आकृतियों में से चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the problem figures the small star moves one corner ahead in each step and the cross, the circle and the square also move one position ahead in the same direction<br>The letter S appears at the lower right in the last problem figure, so in the next figure the star reaches the upper right corner and the other symbols shift by one place<br>Only the first answer figure continues this movement of all four symbols in the same order<br>Hence the first answer figure continues the series<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"समस्या आकृतियों में छोटा तारा प्रत्येक चरण में एक कोना आगे बढ़ता है और क्रॉस, वृत्त तथा वर्ग भी उसी दिशा में एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं<br>अंतिम समस्या आकृति में अक्षर S निचले दाएँ भाग में है, अतः अगली आकृति में तारा ऊपरी दाएँ कोने तक पहुँचता है और शेष चिह्न एक स्थान खिसक जाते हैं<br>केवल पहली उत्तर आकृति में चारों चिह्नों की यही गति क्रम में जारी रहती है<br>अतः पहली उत्तर आकृति श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q25.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072706","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"At which specific Harappan site have archaeologists discovered traces of canals used for irrigation? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस विशिष्ट हड़प्पा स्थल पर पुरातत्वविदों को सिंचाई हेतु प्रयुक्त नहरों के अवशेष मिले हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kalibangan","hi":"कालीबंगन"},"2":{"en":"Dholavira","hi":"धोलावीरा"},"3":{"en":"Shortughai","hi":"शोर्तुघई"},"4":{"en":"Banawali","hi":"बनावली"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Shortughai</b><br>Traces of <b>irrigation canals</b> have been found at <b>Shortughai</b>, a Harappan outpost in north-eastern Afghanistan on the Amu Darya, where a canal was used to irrigate fields around the settlement.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Shortughai is important for its proximity to the <b>lapis lazuli mines of Badakhshan</b> and shows Harappan trade links with Central Asia.<br>• <b>Kalibangan</b> in Rajasthan is famous for its ploughed field and fire altars, and <b>Dholavira</b> in Kutch for its water reservoirs and three-part town planning.<br>• <b>Banawali</b> in Haryana is known for its radial street pattern and barley finds.<br>• Most Harappan irrigation was through <b>inundation canals and wells</b>, and no large canal system like Mesopotamia's has been found in the core Harappan area.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because canal traces were discovered at Shortughai.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – शोर्तुघई</b><br><b>सिंचाई नहरों</b> के अवशेष <b>शोर्तुघई</b> में मिले हैं, जो अफगानिस्तान के उत्तर-पूर्व में आमू दरिया पर स्थित हड़प्पा चौकी थी और जहाँ एक नहर से बस्ती के आसपास के खेतों की सिंचाई होती थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• शोर्तुघई <b>बदख्शां की लापिस लाजुली खदानों</b> की निकटता के कारण महत्वपूर्ण है और यह मध्य एशिया से हड़प्पा व्यापार संबंध दर्शाता है।<br>• राजस्थान का <b>कालीबंगन</b> जुते हुए खेत तथा अग्नि वेदियों के लिए, और कच्छ का <b>धोलावीरा</b> जलाशयों तथा त्रिभागीय नगर नियोजन के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• हरियाणा का <b>बनावली</b> त्रिज्यीय गली-पैटर्न तथा जौ की प्राप्ति के लिए जाना जाता है।<br>• हड़प्पा में सिंचाई मुख्यतः <b>नदी-प्लावन नहरों तथा कुओं</b> से होती थी, और मेसोपोटामिया जैसी बड़ी नहर प्रणाली मुख्य हड़प्पा क्षेत्र में नहीं मिली।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि नहर के अवशेष शोर्तुघई में मिले।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072707","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"Which Sultan of Delhi adopted the title 'Sikandar-i-Sani'? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिल्ली के किस सुल्तान ने 'सिकंदर-ए-सानी' की उपाधि धारण की? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Balban","hi":"बलबन"},"2":{"en":"Alauddin Khalji","hi":"अलाउद्दीन खिलजी"},"3":{"en":"Muhammad-Bin-Tughluq","hi":"मुहम्मद बिन तुगलक"},"4":{"en":"Sikandar Lodi","hi":"सिकंदर लोदी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Alauddin Khalji</b><br><b>Alauddin Khalji</b> assumed the title <b>'Sikandar-i-Sani'</b> (the second Alexander) after his military successes, aspiring to rival Alexander the Great.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Alauddin's achievements include the <b>conquest of Gujarat, Ranthambore, Chittor, Malwa and the Deccan campaigns</b> led by Malik Kafur.<br>• He introduced <b>market control regulations</b>, fixed prices, a standing army paid in cash and the <b>branding of horses (dagh)</b> and descriptive rolls of soldiers (chehra).<br>• <b>Balban</b> took the title 'Zil-i-Ilahi' (shadow of God) and introduced the sijda and paibos customs, while <b>Sikandar Lodi</b> took the title 'Sikandar Shah'.<br>• Alauddin was the first Sultan to maintain a permanent standing army and to measure land for revenue (<b>masahat</b>).<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Alauddin Khalji adopted the title Sikandar-i-Sani.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अलाउद्दीन खिलजी</b><br><b>अलाउद्दीन खिलजी</b> ने अपनी सैन्य सफलताओं के बाद <b>'सिकंदर-ए-सानी'</b> (दूसरा सिकंदर) की उपाधि धारण की, जिससे वे सिकंदर महान के समकक्ष होने की आकांक्षा रखते थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अलाउद्दीन की उपलब्धियों में <b>गुजरात, रणथंभौर, चित्तौड़, मालवा की विजय तथा मलिक काफूर के नेतृत्व में दक्कन अभियान</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• उसने <b>बाजार नियंत्रण विनियम</b>, कीमतें निर्धारित करना, नकद वेतन वाली स्थायी सेना तथा <b>अश्वों का दाग (दाग़)</b> एवं सैनिकों की हुलिया सूची (चेहरा) की प्रथा शुरू की।<br>• <b>बलबन</b> ने 'जिल-ए-इलाही' (ईश्वर की छाया) की उपाधि ली और सिजदा तथा पैबोस की प्रथाएँ शुरू कीं, जबकि <b>सिकंदर लोदी</b> ने 'सिकंदर शाह' उपाधि धारण की।<br>• अलाउद्दीन पहला सुल्तान था जिसने स्थायी सेना रखी तथा राजस्व हेतु भूमि मापी (<b>मसाहत</b>)।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि अलाउद्दीन खिलजी ने सिकंदर-ए-सानी की उपाधि धारण की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072708","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a prominent Middle Palaeolithic site located in Pakistan? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन पाकिस्तान में स्थित एक प्रमुख मध्य पुरापाषाण (Middle Palaeolithic) स्थल है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chirki Nevasa","hi":"चिरकी नेवासा"},"2":{"en":"Kalpi","hi":"काल्पी"},"3":{"en":"Didwana","hi":"डीडवाना"},"4":{"en":"Sanghao cave","hi":"संघाओ गुफा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Sanghao cave</b><br><b>Sanghao cave</b>, in the Mardan district of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa in present-day Pakistan, is a prominent <b>Middle Palaeolithic</b> site excavated in the 1960s, yielding stone tools of that period.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Middle Palaeolithic in the subcontinent is marked by <b>flake and scraper industries</b> and coincides largely with the Middle Stone Age.<br>• <b>Chirki-Nevasa</b> is in Maharashtra and is famous for Lower Palaeolithic handaxes, and <b>Kalpi</b> in Uttar Pradesh is an important Upper Palaeolithic site.<br>• <b>Didwana</b> in Rajasthan is known for its prehistoric stone industries in the Thar region.<br>• Major Middle Palaeolithic sites in India include <b>Bhimabetka, Narmada valley and Kurnool caves</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Sanghao cave in Pakistan is a Middle Palaeolithic site.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – संघाओ गुफा</b><br><b>संघाओ गुफा</b>, जो वर्तमान पाकिस्तान के खैबर पख्तूनख्वा में मरदान जिले में है, एक प्रमुख <b>मध्य पुरापाषाण</b> स्थल है, जिसकी 1960 के दशक में खुदाई हुई और वहाँ उस काल के पाषाण उपकरण मिले।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उपमहाद्वीप में मध्य पुरापाषाण <b>फ्लेक तथा स्क्रेपर उद्योगों</b> से पहचाना जाता है और मोटे तौर पर मध्य पाषाण काल के समकालीन है।<br>• <b>चिरकी-नेवासा</b> महाराष्ट्र में है और निम्न पुरापाषाण के हस्तकुठारों के लिए प्रसिद्ध है, तथा उत्तर प्रदेश का <b>काल्पी</b> उच्च पुरापाषाण का महत्वपूर्ण स्थल है।<br>• राजस्थान का <b>डीडवाना</b> थार क्षेत्र के प्रागैतिहासिक पाषाण उद्योगों के लिए जाना जाता है।<br>• भारत के प्रमुख मध्य पुरापाषाण स्थलों में <b>भीमबेटका, नर्मदा घाटी तथा कुरनूल गुफाएँ</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि पाकिस्तान की संघाओ गुफा मध्य पुरापाषाण स्थल है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072709","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Plateau","question":{"en":"Which physiographic division of India is an irregular triangular region rising from about 150 m above the river plains to an elevation of 600–900 m? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत का कौन-सा भू-आकृतिक विभाग एक अनियमित त्रिभुजाकार क्षेत्र है जो नदी मैदानों से लगभग 150 मीटर की ऊँचाई से उठकर 600–900 मीटर तक पहुँचता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Northern Plains","hi":"उत्तरी मैदान"},"2":{"en":"Himalayan Mountains","hi":"हिमालय पर्वत"},"3":{"en":"Peninsular Plateau","hi":"प्रायद्वीपीय पठार"},"4":{"en":"Coastal Plains","hi":"तटीय मैदान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Peninsular Plateau</b><br>The <b>Peninsular Plateau</b> of India is an irregular <b>triangular</b> tableland that rises from about <b>150 m above the river plains to 600-900 m</b> elevation, and is one of the oldest and most stable landmasses of the earth.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It is bounded by the <b>Aravallis in the north-west, the Rajmahal hills in the east and the Western and Eastern Ghats</b> in the south.<br>• The plateau consists of the <b>Malwa plateau, Bundelkhand, Baghelkhand, Chotanagpur plateau and the Deccan trap region</b>.<br>• It was formerly part of <b>Gondwanaland</b> and is made largely of ancient Archaean gneisses and schists, with black cotton soil in the Deccan trap area.<br>• The Northern Plains and coastal plains lie below 200 m, and the Himalayas rise above 5,000 m, so neither matches the described elevation.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the described triangular region rising to 600-900 m is the Peninsular Plateau.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रायद्वीपीय पठार</b><br>भारत का <b>प्रायद्वीपीय पठार</b> एक अनियमित <b>त्रिभुजाकार</b> मेज़ानुमा भूभाग है, जो नदी मैदानों से लगभग <b>150 मीटर की ऊँचाई से उठकर 600-900 मीटर</b> तक पहुँचता है और पृथ्वी के प्राचीनतम तथा स्थिरतम भूभागों में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी सीमा उत्तर-पश्चिम में <b>अरावली, पूर्व में राजमहल पहाड़ियाँ तथा दक्षिण में पश्चिमी एवं पूर्वी घाट</b> से बनती है।<br>• इस पठार में <b>मालवा पठार, बुंदेलखंड, बाघेलखंड, छोटानागपुर पठार तथा दक्कन ट्रैप क्षेत्र</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• यह पहले <b>गोंडवानालैंड</b> का भाग था और मुख्यतः प्राचीन आर्कियन नीस तथा शिस्ट से बना है, तथा दक्कन ट्रैप क्षेत्र में काली कपास मिट्टी है।<br>• उत्तरी मैदान तथा तटीय मैदान 200 मीटर से नीचे हैं, और हिमालय 5,000 मीटर से ऊपर उठता है, इसलिए वर्णित ऊँचाई से कोई मेल नहीं खाता।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 600-900 मीटर तक उठने वाला त्रिभुजाकार क्षेत्र प्रायद्वीपीय पठार है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072710","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Which statement <b>correctly</b> identifies the mechanism behind isostatic equilibrium in the Earth’s crust? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन पृथ्वी की परत में समस्थितिक संतुलन (isostatic equilibrium) के तंत्र को <b>सही</b> ढंग से पहचानता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mantle convection prevents crustal vertical movement.","hi":"मैंटल संवहन परत की ऊर्ध्वाधर गति को रोकता है।"},"2":{"en":"Mountains maintain height via volcanic core pressure.","hi":"पर्वत ज्वालामुखीय कोर दाब से ऊँचाई बनाए रखते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Crustal sections float based on density differences.","hi":"परत के खंड घनत्व अंतर के आधार पर तैरते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Erosion increases the thickness of mountain roots.","hi":"अपरदन से पर्वत-जड़ की मोटाई बढ़ती है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Crustal sections float based on density differences.</b><br><b>Isostasy</b> is the state of gravitational equilibrium in which the earth's crustal blocks <b>float on the denser mantle</b> according to their <b>density and thickness</b>, so that higher mountains have deeper 'roots'.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Airy</b> model explains isostasy through differences in crustal thickness, and the <b>Pratt</b> model through differences in density.<br>• Post-glacial rebound in Scandinavia and the rise of land after erosion are examples of isostatic adjustment.<br>• <b>Erosion reduces</b> the load and causes the mountain root to rise, so option (4) is reversed; mantle convection drives plate motion rather than preventing vertical movement.<br>• Isostasy explains why the earth's gravity is nearly uniform across mountains and oceans, which puzzled early surveyors in India.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because crustal sections float according to density differences.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – परत के खंड घनत्व अंतर के आधार पर तैरते हैं।</b><br><b>समस्थिति (Isostasy)</b> गुरुत्वीय संतुलन की वह अवस्था है जिसमें पृथ्वी के परत-खंड अपने <b>घनत्व तथा मोटाई</b> के अनुसार <b>अधिक घनत्व वाले मैंटल पर तैरते</b> हैं, इसलिए ऊँचे पर्वतों की 'जड़ें' अधिक गहरी होती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>एरी</b> प्रतिरूप समस्थिति को परत की मोटाई के अंतर से तथा <b>प्रैट</b> प्रतिरूप घनत्व के अंतर से समझाता है।<br>• स्कैंडिनेविया में हिमनद-पश्चात उत्थान तथा अपरदन के बाद भूमि का उठना समस्थितिक समायोजन के उदाहरण हैं।<br>• <b>अपरदन भार घटाता</b> है और पर्वत-जड़ को ऊपर उठाता है, इसलिए विकल्प (4) उलटा है; मैंटल संवहन प्लेट गति चलाता है, ऊर्ध्वाधर गति नहीं रोकता।<br>• समस्थिति यह समझाती है कि पर्वतों तथा महासागरों पर पृथ्वी का गुरुत्व लगभग समान क्यों रहता है, जिससे भारत के आरंभिक सर्वेक्षणकर्ता चकित हुए थे।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि परत के खंड घनत्व अंतर के अनुसार तैरते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072711","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Transport","question":{"en":"Which of the following stretches is covered under National Waterway 2 (NW-2) in India? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग 2 (NW-2) के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विस्तार आता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prayagraj–Haldia stretch","hi":"प्रयागराज–हल्दिया विस्तार"},"2":{"en":"Sadiya–Dhubri stretch","hi":"सदिया–धुबरी विस्तार"},"3":{"en":"Kottapuram–Kollam stretch","hi":"कोट्टापुरम–कोल्लम विस्तार"},"4":{"en":"Haldia–Sadiya stretch","hi":"हल्दिया–सदिया विस्तार"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sadiya–Dhubri stretch</b><br><b>National Waterway 2 (NW-2)</b> is the <b>Sadiya-Dhubri stretch of the Brahmaputra river</b> in Assam, about <b>891 km</b> long, and is one of the five waterways declared in 1986.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>NW-1</b> is the <b>Prayagraj-Haldia stretch</b> of the Ganga (about 1,620 km), developed as the Jal Marg Vikas Project.<br>• <b>NW-3</b> is the West Coast Canal from <b>Kottapuram to Kollam</b> in Kerala, along with the Champakara and Udyogmandal canals.<br>• NW-4 covers the Godavari-Krishna delta and NW-5 the Brahmani-Mahanadi delta in Odisha.<br>• The <b>Inland Waterways Authority of India</b>, set up in 1986, develops and maintains national waterways for cargo and passenger transport.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because NW-2 is the Sadiya-Dhubri stretch of the Brahmaputra.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सदिया–धुबरी विस्तार</b><br><b>राष्ट्रीय जलमार्ग 2 (NW-2)</b> असम में <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र नदी का सदिया-धुबरी विस्तार</b> है, जो लगभग <b>891 किमी</b> लंबा है और 1986 में घोषित पाँच जलमार्गों में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>NW-1</b> गंगा का <b>प्रयागराज-हल्दिया विस्तार</b> (लगभग 1,620 किमी) है, जिसे जल मार्ग विकास परियोजना के अंतर्गत विकसित किया जा रहा है।<br>• <b>NW-3</b> केरल में <b>कोट्टापुरम से कोल्लम</b> तक पश्चिमी तट नहर है, साथ ही चंपाकारा तथा उद्योगमंडल नहरें।<br>• NW-4 गोदावरी-कृष्णा डेल्टा तथा NW-5 ओडिशा में ब्राह्मणी-महानदी डेल्टा को समेटता है।<br>• 1986 में गठित <b>अंतर्देशीय जलमार्ग प्राधिकरण</b> राष्ट्रीय जलमार्गों को माल तथा यात्री परिवहन हेतु विकसित एवं अनुरक्षित करता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि NW-2 ब्रह्मपुत्र का सदिया-धुबरी विस्तार है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072712","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"In which of the following states is the Chapchar Kut festival primarily celebrated? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चापचार कुट उत्सव मुख्यतः किस राज्य में मनाया जाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nagaland","hi":"नागालैंड"},"2":{"en":"Mizoram","hi":"मिज़ोरम"},"3":{"en":"Assam","hi":"असम"},"4":{"en":"Manipur","hi":"मणिपुर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Mizoram</b><br><b>Chapchar Kut</b> is the biggest and most colourful festival of <b>Mizoram</b>, celebrated in March after the clearing of the jhum fields, with the traditional <b>Cheraw</b> (bamboo) dance and community feasts.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Mizo festivals associated with jhum cultivation are <b>Chapchar Kut (spring), Mim Kut (maize harvest) and Pawl Kut (harvest)</b>.<br>• <b>Cheraw</b> is the bamboo dance of Mizoram, and other Mizo dances are Khuallam and Chheihlam.<br>• Nagaland's major festival is the <b>Hornbill Festival</b>, Assam's are <b>Bihu</b>, and Manipur's include <b>Yaoshang and Ningol Chakouba</b>.<br>• Chapchar Kut is declared a state holiday in Mizoram and is celebrated with the 'Kut' festival spirit of gratitude after the clearing of forests for cultivation.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Chapchar Kut is primarily celebrated in Mizoram.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मिज़ोरम</b><br><b>चापचार कुट</b> <b>मिज़ोरम</b> का सबसे बड़ा तथा सर्वाधिक रंगीन उत्सव है, जो झूम खेतों की सफाई के बाद मार्च में पारंपरिक <b>चेराव</b> (बाँस) नृत्य तथा सामूहिक भोज के साथ मनाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• झूम खेती से जुड़े मिज़ो उत्सव हैं – <b>चापचार कुट (वसंत), मिम कुट (मक्का कटाई) तथा पावल कुट (फसल)</b>।<br>• <b>चेराव</b> मिज़ोरम का बाँस नृत्य है, तथा अन्य मिज़ो नृत्य खुआल्लम एवं छेइहलम हैं।<br>• नागालैंड का प्रमुख उत्सव <b>हॉर्नबिल महोत्सव</b>, असम का <b>बिहू</b>, तथा मणिपुर के उत्सवों में <b>याओशांग एवं निंगोल चाकोउबा</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• चापचार कुट मिज़ोरम में राजकीय अवकाश है और खेती हेतु वन साफ करने के बाद कृतज्ञता के 'कुट' भाव से मनाया जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि चापचार कुट मुख्यतः मिज़ोरम में मनाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072713","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"As of 2026, M. Jagadesh Kumar completed his tenure as the head of which statutory education body in India? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2026 तक एम. जगदीश कुमार ने भारत के किस सांविधिक शिक्षा निकाय के प्रमुख के रूप में अपना कार्यकाल पूरा किया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jawaharlal Nehru University (JNU)","hi":"जवाहरलाल नेहरू विश्वविद्यालय (JNU)"},"2":{"en":"University Grants Commission (UGC)","hi":"विश्वविद्यालय अनुदान आयोग (UGC)"},"3":{"en":"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)","hi":"राष्ट्रीय शैक्षिक अनुसंधान एवं प्रशिक्षण परिषद (NCERT)"},"4":{"en":"Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU)","hi":"इंदिरा गांधी राष्ट्रीय मुक्त विश्वविद्यालय (IGNOU)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – University Grants Commission (UGC)</b><br><b>M. Jagadesh Kumar</b> served as the <b>Chairman of the University Grants Commission (UGC)</b> from <b>February 2022</b> and completed his tenure in 2026, having earlier been Vice-Chancellor of JNU.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The UGC is a <b>statutory body</b> set up under the UGC Act, 1956, and coordinates, determines and maintains standards of higher education.<br>• Jagadesh Kumar is an academic and researcher in electronics and served as <b>Vice-Chancellor of JNU (2016-2022)</b>.<br>• During his tenure the UGC implemented the <b>National Education Policy 2020 reforms, the four-year undergraduate programme and new appointment regulations</b>.<br>• <b>NCERT</b> is an autonomous body under the Ministry of Education, and <b>IGNOU</b> is a central open university, not a statutory regulator.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because M. Jagadesh Kumar headed the UGC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विश्वविद्यालय अनुदान आयोग (UGC)</b><br><b>एम. जगदीश कुमार (M. Jagadesh Kumar)</b> ने <b>फरवरी 2022</b> से <b>विश्वविद्यालय अनुदान आयोग (UGC) के अध्यक्ष</b> के रूप में कार्य किया और 2026 में उनका कार्यकाल पूरा हुआ, इससे पूर्व वे JNU के कुलपति थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• UGC <b>UGC अधिनियम, 1956</b> के अंतर्गत गठित <b>सांविधिक निकाय</b> है, जो उच्च शिक्षा के मानकों का समन्वय, निर्धारण तथा अनुरक्षण करता है।<br>• जगदीश कुमार इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स के शिक्षाविद् एवं शोधकर्ता हैं तथा <b>JNU के कुलपति (2016-2022)</b> रहे।<br>• उनके कार्यकाल में UGC ने <b>राष्ट्रीय शिक्षा नीति 2020 के सुधार, चार-वर्षीय स्नातक कार्यक्रम तथा नई नियुक्ति विनियम</b> लागू किए।<br>• <b>NCERT</b> शिक्षा मंत्रालय के अधीन स्वायत्त निकाय है, और <b>IGNOU</b> केंद्रीय मुक्त विश्वविद्यालय है, सांविधिक नियामक नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि एम. जगदीश कुमार UGC के प्रमुख थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072714","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"In 2024, former Union Health Secretary of India Preeti Sudan was appointed to which position? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2024 में भारत के पूर्व संघ स्वास्थ्य सचिव प्रीति सूदन को किस पद पर नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Member of NITI (National Institution for Transforming India) Aayog","hi":"नीति आयोग के सदस्य"},"2":{"en":"Chairperson of Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)","hi":"संघ लोक सेवा आयोग (UPSC) के अध्यक्ष"},"3":{"en":"Secretary to the President of India","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रपति के सचिव"},"4":{"en":"Chairperson of Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI)","hi":"भारतीय खाद्य संरक्षा एवं मानक प्राधिकरण (FSSAI) के अध्यक्ष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chairperson of Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)</b><br>In <b>2024</b>, former Union Health Secretary <b>Preeti Sudan</b> was appointed <b>Chairperson of the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)</b>, succeeding Manoj Soni.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Preeti Sudan is a <b>1983-batch IAS officer of the Andhra Pradesh cadre</b> and served as Health Secretary during the COVID-19 pandemic.<br>• She was India's representative on the <b>GAVI Board</b> and worked with the World Bank and UNICEF before joining the IAS.<br>• The UPSC Chairman is appointed by the <b>President</b> under Article 316 and holds office for six years or until 65 years of age.<br>• The UPSC is a <b>constitutional body</b> established under Article 315 and conducts the Civil Services Examination and other recruitments.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Preeti Sudan was appointed UPSC Chairperson in 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – संघ लोक सेवा आयोग (UPSC) के अध्यक्ष</b><br><b>2024</b> में पूर्व संघ स्वास्थ्य सचिव <b>प्रीति सूदन (Preeti Sudan)</b> को मनोज सोनी के स्थान पर <b>संघ लोक सेवा आयोग (UPSC) का अध्यक्ष</b> नियुक्त किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रीति सूदन <b>आंध्र प्रदेश कैडर की 1983 बैच की IAS अधिकारी</b> हैं और कोविड-19 महामारी के समय स्वास्थ्य सचिव रहीं।<br>• वे <b>GAVI बोर्ड</b> में भारत की प्रतिनिधि रहीं तथा IAS में आने से पहले विश्व बैंक एवं UNICEF के साथ कार्य किया।<br>• UPSC अध्यक्ष की नियुक्ति <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> अनुच्छेद 316 के अंतर्गत करता है और कार्यकाल छह वर्ष या 65 वर्ष की आयु तक होता है।<br>• UPSC <b>अनुच्छेद 315</b> के अंतर्गत स्थापित <b>संवैधानिक निकाय</b> है, जो सिविल सेवा परीक्षा तथा अन्य भर्तियाँ करता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि 2024 में प्रीति सूदन UPSC अध्यक्ष नियुक्त हुईं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072715","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The Namo Drone Didi scheme provides drones to women Self-Help Groups primarily to help them offer which service? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नमो ड्रोन दीदी योजना महिला स्वयं सहायता समूहों को मुख्यतः कौन-सी सेवा देने हेतु ड्रोन प्रदान करती है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Conducting aerial mapping of forest areas","hi":"वन क्षेत्रों का हवाई मानचित्रण करना"},"2":{"en":"Delivering emergency medical supplies in villages","hi":"गाँवों में आपातकालीन चिकित्सा आपूर्ति पहुँचाना"},"3":{"en":"Providing drone rental services to farmers for agricultural operations","hi":"कृषि कार्यों हेतु किसानों को ड्रोन किराये की सेवा देना"},"4":{"en":"Monitoring urban traffic and infrastructure","hi":"शहरी यातायात तथा अवसंरचना की निगरानी करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Providing drone rental services to farmers for agricultural operations</b><br>The <b>Namo Drone Didi</b> scheme provides drones to <b>women Self-Help Groups</b> so that they can offer <b>drone rental services to farmers</b> for spraying fertilisers and pesticides, generating income for the SHGs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The scheme was launched in <b>2023-24</b> and aims to provide drones to <b>15,000 women SHGs</b>, along with training for 'drone didis' as pilots and technicians.<br>• It is implemented by the <b>Department of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare</b> with the Ministry of Rural Development.<br>• Financial support covers about <b>80% of the drone cost</b>, up to ₹8 lakh, with a maximum of ₹8 lakh per SHG for the drone and accessories.<br>• Benefits include <b>reduced water and pesticide use, faster spraying and additional income</b> of about ₹1 lakh per year for the SHG.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the scheme helps SHGs provide drone rental services to farmers.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कृषि कार्यों हेतु किसानों को ड्रोन किराये की सेवा देना</b><br><b>नमो ड्रोन दीदी</b> योजना <b>महिला स्वयं सहायता समूहों</b> को ड्रोन देती है, जिससे वे उर्वरक तथा कीटनाशक छिड़काव हेतु <b>किसानों को ड्रोन किराये की सेवा</b> दे सकें और समूहों को आय हो।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना <b>2023-24</b> में शुरू हुई और इसका लक्ष्य <b>15,000 महिला स्वयं सहायता समूहों</b> को ड्रोन देना है, साथ ही 'ड्रोन दीदी' को पायलट तथा तकनीशियन का प्रशिक्षण दिया जाता है।<br>• इसे <b>कृषि एवं किसान कल्याण विभाग</b> ग्रामीण विकास मंत्रालय के साथ क्रियान्वित करता है।<br>• वित्तीय सहायता ड्रोन की लागत का लगभग <b>80%</b>, अधिकतम ₹8 लाख तक, तथा ड्रोन एवं सहायक उपकरणों के लिए प्रति समूह अधिकतम ₹8 लाख है।<br>• लाभों में <b>जल एवं कीटनाशक की कम खपत, तेज छिड़काव तथा समूह को प्रतिवर्ष लगभग ₹1 लाख की अतिरिक्त आय</b> सम्मिलित है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि योजना समूहों को किसानों को ड्रोन किराये पर देने में सहायता करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072716","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which of the following authors received the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025 for the Short Stories collection “Mid Birna Chenne Saon Inag Sagai”? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित लेखकों में से किसे कहानी संग्रह \"मिड बिरना चेन्ने साओन इनाग सागई\" के लिए साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 प्राप्त हुआ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bhagwan Atlani","hi":"भगवान अटलानी"},"2":{"en":"Prakash Bhattarai","hi":"प्रकाश भट्टराई"},"3":{"en":"Sahaisuli Brahma","hi":"सहाइसुली ब्रह्मा"},"4":{"en":"Sumitra Soren","hi":"सुमित्रा सोरेन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Sumitra Soren</b><br><b>Sumitra Soren</b> received the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b> for <b>Santali</b> for her short-story collection <b>'Mid Birna Chenne Saon Inag Sagai'</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 2025 awards covered <b>24 Indian languages</b>, with eight poetry, four novel, six short-story, two essay, one literary criticism, one autobiography and two memoir awards.<br>• <b>Bhagwan Atlani</b> won for Sindhi ('Waghoo') and <b>Sahaisuli Brahma</b> for Bodo ('Dwngnwi Lama Mwnse Gathwn'), while <b>Prakash Bhattarai</b> was not among the 2025 awardees.<br>• The Sahitya Akademi, established in <b>1954</b>, is an autonomous body under the Ministry of Culture and gives awards in 24 recognised languages including English and Rajasthani.<br>• Each award carries a plaque, a shawl and a cash prize of <b>₹1 lakh</b>, and the 2025 awards were to be presented on 31 March 2026.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Sumitra Soren won the 2025 award for the Santali short-story collection.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – सुमित्रा सोरेन</b><br><b>सुमित्रा सोरेन (Sumitra Soren)</b> को कहानी संग्रह <b>'मिड बिरना चेन्ने साओन इनाग सागई'</b> के लिए <b>संताली</b> भाषा में <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2025 के पुरस्कार <b>24 भारतीय भाषाओं</b> में दिए गए, जिनमें आठ काव्य, चार उपन्यास, छह कहानी संग्रह, दो निबंध, एक साहित्यिक आलोचना, एक आत्मकथा तथा दो संस्मरण थे।<br>• <b>भगवान अटलानी</b> को सिंधी ('वाघू') तथा <b>सहाइसुली ब्रह्मा</b> को बोडो ('द्वंगन्वी लामा म्वन्से गथ्वन') के लिए पुरस्कार मिला, जबकि <b>प्रकाश भट्टराई</b> 2025 के पुरस्कार विजेताओं में नहीं थे।<br>• 1954 में स्थापित साहित्य अकादमी संस्कृति मंत्रालय के अधीन स्वायत्त निकाय है और अंग्रेज़ी तथा राजस्थानी सहित 24 मान्यता प्राप्त भाषाओं में पुरस्कार देती है।<br>• प्रत्येक पुरस्कार में ताम्रपत्र, शॉल तथा <b>₹1 लाख</b> की राशि मिलती है, और 2025 के पुरस्कार 31 मार्च 2026 को प्रदान किए जाने थे।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि संताली कहानी संग्रह के लिए सुमित्रा सोरेन को 2025 का पुरस्कार मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072717","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Plateau","question":{"en":"Which hill range lies at the centre of the Satpura system? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"सतपुड़ा प्रणाली के केंद्र में कौन-सी पहाड़ी श्रेणी स्थित है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maikal Hills","hi":"मैकल पहाड़ियाँ"},"2":{"en":"Parasnath Hills","hi":"पारसनाथ पहाड़ियाँ"},"3":{"en":"Rajpipla Hills","hi":"राजपीपला पहाड़ियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Mahadeo Hills","hi":"महादेव पहाड़ियाँ"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Mahadeo Hills</b><br>The <b>Mahadeo Hills</b> lie at the <b>centre of the Satpura system</b>, running east-west across southern Madhya Pradesh, with <b>Dhupgarh</b> as their highest peak near Pachmarhi.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Satpura range extends from the <b>Rajpipla hills in Gujarat</b> in the west through the <b>Mahadeo and Maikal hills</b> to the <b>Chotanagpur plateau</b> in the east.<br>• <b>Dhupgarh (1,350 m)</b> is the highest peak of the Satpura and of Madhya Pradesh, and Pachmarhi is a hill station on the Mahadeo hills.<br>• The <b>Maikal hills</b> form the eastern part of the Satpura and separate the Narmada from the Mahanadi basin.<br>• The <b>Parasnath hills</b> in Jharkhand are part of the Chotanagpur plateau and are a Jain pilgrimage centre.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the Mahadeo Hills lie at the centre of the Satpura system.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – महादेव पहाड़ियाँ</b><br><b>महादेव पहाड़ियाँ</b> <b>सतपुड़ा प्रणाली के केंद्र</b> में स्थित हैं और दक्षिणी मध्य प्रदेश में पूर्व-पश्चिम फैली हैं, जिनका सर्वोच्च शिखर पचमढ़ी के निकट <b>धूपगढ़</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सतपुड़ा श्रेणी पश्चिम में गुजरात की <b>राजपीपला पहाड़ियों</b> से <b>महादेव तथा मैकल पहाड़ियों</b> के रास्ते पूर्व में <b>छोटानागपुर पठार</b> तक फैली है।<br>• <b>धूपगढ़ (1,350 मीटर)</b> सतपुड़ा तथा मध्य प्रदेश का सर्वोच्च शिखर है, और पचमढ़ी महादेव पहाड़ियों पर स्थित हिल स्टेशन है।<br>• <b>मैकल पहाड़ियाँ</b> सतपुड़ा का पूर्वी भाग बनाती हैं और नर्मदा को महानदी बेसिन से अलग करती हैं।<br>• झारखंड की <b>पारसनाथ पहाड़ियाँ</b> छोटानागपुर पठार का भाग हैं और जैन तीर्थ केंद्र हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि महादेव पहाड़ियाँ सतपुड़ा प्रणाली के केंद्र में हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072718","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A state government issues a notification applying only Chapters IX and XI of the BNSS (Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita), 2023 to certain tribal areas previously excluded under Section 1(2). A lawyer argues that such notification is invalid because excluded areas can never be brought within BNSS applicability. Which option is legally correct? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक राज्य सरकार अधिसूचना जारी करके भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता (BNSS), 2023 के केवल अध्याय IX तथा XI को उन अनुसूचित जनजातीय क्षेत्रों पर लागू करती है जो पहले धारा 1(2) के अंतर्गत बाहर रखे गए थे। एक अधिवक्ता तर्क देता है कि ऐसी अधिसूचना अवैध है क्योंकि बहिष्कृत क्षेत्रों को कभी BNSS के दायरे में नहीं लाया जा सकता। कौन-सा विकल्प विधिक रूप से सही है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The lawyer is correct because tribal areas are permanently exempt.","hi":"अधिवक्ता सही है क्योंकि जनजातीय क्षेत्र स्थायी रूप से छूट प्राप्त हैं।"},"2":{"en":"The notification is invalid unless Parliament separately approves it.","hi":"अधिसूचना अवैध है जब तक संसद अलग से स्वीकृति न दे।"},"3":{"en":"BNSS (Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita) provisions can be applied by state notification with changes.","hi":"BNSS के प्रावधान राज्य अधिसूचना द्वारा परिवर्तनों के साथ लागू किए जा सकते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only the central government may extend BNSS (Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita) to tribal areas.","hi":"केवल केंद्र सरकार BNSS को जनजातीय क्षेत्रों तक विस्तारित कर सकती है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – BNSS (Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita) provisions can be applied by state notification with changes.</b><br>Under <b>Section 1(2) of the BNSS, 2023</b>, the provisions do not apply to <b>Scheduled Areas and tribal areas</b> unless the <b>State Government</b> by notification applies them, and such a notification may apply them <b>with such exceptions and modifications as it specifies</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The exemption is <b>not permanent</b>, and the state government has the power to extend any or all chapters to such areas by notification.<br>• The provision ensures respect for <b>customary law and tribal autonomy</b> under the Fifth and Sixth Schedules of the Constitution.<br>• The notification can apply <b>only Chapters IX and XI</b>, which deal with evidence and bail-related matters, as described in the question.<br>• Neither Parliament's separate approval nor the central government's action is required, so options (1), (2) and (4) are wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the state government may apply BNSS provisions by notification with changes.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – BNSS के प्रावधान राज्य अधिसूचना द्वारा परिवर्तनों के साथ लागू किए जा सकते हैं।</b><br><b>BNSS, 2023 की धारा 1(2)</b> के अंतर्गत ये प्रावधान <b>अनुसूचित क्षेत्रों तथा जनजातीय क्षेत्रों</b> पर लागू नहीं होते, जब तक <b>राज्य सरकार</b> अधिसूचना द्वारा उन्हें लागू न करे, और ऐसी अधिसूचना उन्हें <b>निर्दिष्ट अपवादों तथा संशोधनों के साथ</b> लागू कर सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह छूट <b>स्थायी नहीं</b> है, और राज्य सरकार को अधिसूचना द्वारा कोई भी या सभी अध्याय ऐसे क्षेत्रों तक विस्तारित करने की शक्ति है।<br>• यह प्रावधान संविधान की पाँचवीं तथा छठी अनुसूची के अंतर्गत <b>प्रथागत विधि तथा जनजातीय स्वायत्तता</b> का सम्मान सुनिश्चित करता है।<br>• अधिसूचना <b>केवल अध्याय IX तथा XI</b> लागू कर सकती है, जो साक्ष्य तथा जमानत-संबंधी विषयों से संबंधित हैं, जैसा प्रश्न में वर्णित है।<br>• न संसद की अलग स्वीकृति आवश्यक है, न केंद्र सरकार की कार्रवाई, इसलिए विकल्प (1), (2) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि राज्य सरकार अधिसूचना द्वारा परिवर्तनों के साथ BNSS प्रावधान लागू कर सकती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072719","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was appointed as the 26<sup>th</sup> Governor of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) in December 2024, succeeding Shaktikanta Das? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिसंबर 2024 में शक्तिकांत दास के स्थान पर भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक (RBI) के 26वें गवर्नर के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Urjit Patel","hi":"उर्जित पटेल"},"2":{"en":"Sanjay Malhotra","hi":"संजय मल्होत्रा"},"3":{"en":"T.V. Somanathan","hi":"टी. वी. सोमनाथन"},"4":{"en":"Raghuram Rajan","hi":"रघुराम राजन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sanjay Malhotra</b><br><b>Sanjay Malhotra</b>, then Revenue Secretary, was appointed the <b>26th Governor of the Reserve Bank of India</b> in <b>December 2024</b>, succeeding <b>Shaktikanta Das</b>, for a three-year term.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Sanjay Malhotra is a <b>1990-batch IAS officer of the Rajasthan cadre</b> and has served in the Departments of Financial Services, Revenue and Economic Affairs.<br>• <b>Shaktikanta Das</b> was RBI Governor from 2018 to 2024 and later became Principal Secretary to the Prime Minister.<br>• <b>Urjit Patel</b> was Governor from 2016 to 2018 and <b>Raghuram Rajan</b> from 2013 to 2016.<br>• The RBI Governor is appointed by the <b>Central Government</b> under the RBI Act, 1934 and holds office for up to three years, with a maximum age limit of 64.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Sanjay Malhotra became the 26th RBI Governor in December 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – संजय मल्होत्रा</b><br>तत्कालीन राजस्व सचिव <b>संजय मल्होत्रा (Sanjay Malhotra)</b> को <b>दिसंबर 2024</b> में <b>शक्तिकांत दास</b> के स्थान पर <b>भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के 26वें गवर्नर</b> के रूप में तीन वर्ष के कार्यकाल हेतु नियुक्त किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• संजय मल्होत्रा <b>राजस्थान कैडर के 1990 बैच के IAS अधिकारी</b> हैं और वित्तीय सेवाएँ, राजस्व तथा आर्थिक मामलों के विभागों में कार्यरत रहे।<br>• <b>शक्तिकांत दास</b> 2018 से 2024 तक RBI गवर्नर रहे और बाद में प्रधानमंत्री के प्रधान सचिव बने।<br>• <b>उर्जित पटेल</b> 2016 से 2018 तक तथा <b>रघुराम राजन</b> 2013 से 2016 तक गवर्नर रहे।<br>• RBI गवर्नर की नियुक्ति <b>केंद्र सरकार</b> RBI अधिनियम, 1934 के अंतर्गत करती है और कार्यकाल अधिकतम तीन वर्ष तथा अधिकतम आयु 64 वर्ष होती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि दिसंबर 2024 में संजय मल्होत्रा 26वें RBI गवर्नर बने।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072720","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which tribal woman from Karnataka, known as the “Encyclopedia of the Forest,” was awarded the Padma Shri? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कर्नाटक की कौन-सी जनजातीय महिला, जिन्हें \"वन की विश्वकोश\" कहा जाता है, को पद्म श्री प्रदान किया गया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tulsi Gowda","hi":"तुलसी गौड़ा"},"2":{"en":"Saalu Marada Thimmakka","hi":"सालुमरद थिम्मक्का"},"3":{"en":"Sudha Murty","hi":"सुधा मूर्ति"},"4":{"en":"Medha Patkar","hi":"मेधा पाटकर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Tulsi Gowda</b><br><b>Tulsi Gowda</b>, a tribal environmentalist from Karnataka's Uttara Kannada district, was awarded the <b>Padma Shri in 2020</b> for planting and nurturing lakhs of trees and is known as the <b>'Encyclopedia of the Forest'</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She belongs to the <b>Halakki Vokkaliga tribal community</b> and has worked with the Karnataka forest department on afforestation and seed collection.<br>• She had earlier received the <b>Indira Priyadarshini Vrikshamitra Award</b> and the Rajyotsava Award.<br>• <b>Saalumarada Thimmakka</b> is another Karnataka environmentalist known for planting banyan trees along roads, and <b>Sudha Murty</b> is a writer and philanthropist.<br>• <b>Medha Patkar</b> is a social activist associated with the Narmada Bachao Andolan.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Tulsi Gowda is known as the Encyclopedia of the Forest.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – तुलसी गौड़ा</b><br>कर्नाटक के उत्तर कन्नड़ जिले की जनजातीय पर्यावरणविद् <b>तुलसी गौड़ा (Tulsi Gowda)</b> को लाखों वृक्ष लगाने तथा उनकी देखभाल के लिए <b>2020 में पद्म श्री</b> प्रदान किया गया, और उन्हें <b>'वन की विश्वकोश'</b> कहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे <b>हलक्की वोक्कालिगा जनजातीय समुदाय</b> से हैं और उन्होंने कर्नाटक वन विभाग के साथ वनीकरण तथा बीज संग्रह का कार्य किया।<br>• उन्हें पहले <b>इंदिरा प्रियदर्शिनी वृक्षमित्र पुरस्कार</b> तथा राज्योत्सव पुरस्कार मिल चुका है।<br>• <b>सालुमरद थिम्मक्का</b> कर्नाटक की दूसरी पर्यावरणविद् हैं जो सड़कों के किनारे बरगद लगाने के लिए जानी जाती हैं, तथा <b>सुधा मूर्ति</b> लेखिका एवं परोपकारी हैं।<br>• <b>मेधा पाटकर</b> नर्मदा बचाओ आंदोलन से जुड़ी सामाजिक कार्यकर्ता हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि तुलसी गौड़ा को वन की विश्वकोश कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072721","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"Which distinct structural ground plan characterizes the prominent ancient temples excavated at the historical site of Nagarjunakonda? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नागार्जुनकोंडा के ऐतिहासिक स्थल पर उत्खनित प्रमुख प्राचीन मंदिरों की विशिष्ट संरचनात्मक भू-योजना कौन-सी है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Apsidal horseshoe plan","hi":"अर्धवृत्ताकार अश्वखुर (apsidal) योजना"},"2":{"en":"Rectangular cruciform plan","hi":"आयताकार क्रूसाकार योजना"},"3":{"en":"Octagonal concentric plan","hi":"अष्टकोणीय संकेंद्रित योजना"},"4":{"en":"Square stellate plan","hi":"वर्गाकार तारकीय योजना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Apsidal horseshoe plan</b><br>The early Buddhist temples excavated at <b>Nagarjunakonda</b> in Andhra Pradesh have an <b>apsidal or horseshoe-shaped ground plan</b>, with a circular rear and a rectangular front, a form continued from earlier chaitya architecture.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Nagarjunakonda was the capital of the <b>Ikshvaku dynasty</b> in the 3rd-4th century CE and is named after <b>Acharya Nagarjuna</b>, the Buddhist philosopher.<br>• The site has numerous <b>Buddhist stupas, viharas, chaityas and a Roman coin hoard</b>, showing trade with the Roman empire.<br>• The excavated structures were relocated to higher ground when the Nagarjuna Sagar dam submerged the valley.<br>• The apsidal plan later evolved into the <b>garbhagriha with a shikhara</b> in the Dravidian temple style.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the Nagarjunakonda temples have an apsidal horseshoe plan.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अर्धवृत्ताकार अश्वखुर (apsidal) योजना</b><br>आंध्र प्रदेश में <b>नागार्जुनकोंडा</b> में उत्खनित प्रारंभिक बौद्ध मंदिरों की <b>अर्धवृत्ताकार या अश्वखुर आकार की भू-योजना</b> है, जिसका पिछला भाग वृत्ताकार तथा अगला भाग आयताकार होता है; यह रूप पूर्ववर्ती चैत्य वास्तुकला से आगे बढ़ा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नागार्जुनकोंडा तीसरी-चौथी शताब्दी ईस्वी में <b>इक्ष्वाकु राजवंश</b> की राजधानी था और इसका नाम बौद्ध दार्शनिक <b>आचार्य नागार्जुन</b> पर पड़ा।<br>• यहाँ अनेक <b>बौद्ध स्तूप, विहार, चैत्य तथा रोमन सिक्कों का भंडार</b> मिला, जो रोमन साम्राज्य से व्यापार दर्शाता है।<br>• नागार्जुन सागर बाँध से घाटी जलमग्न होने पर उत्खनित संरचनाओं को ऊँची भूमि पर स्थानांतरित किया गया।<br>• अश्वखुर योजना बाद में द्रविड़ मंदिर शैली में <b>शिखर सहित गर्भगृह</b> के रूप में विकसित हुई।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि नागार्जुनकोंडा के मंदिरों की योजना अर्धवृत्ताकार अश्वखुर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072722","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"On which date did the Syed Modi India International 2025, part of the Badminton World Federation (BWF) World Tour Super 300 series, come to an end? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बैडमिंटन विश्व महासंघ (BWF) विश्व टूर सुपर 300 श्रृंखला के अंतर्गत सैयद मोदी इंडिया इंटरनेशनल 2025 किस तिथि को समाप्त हुआ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"28 November 2025","hi":"28 नवंबर 2025"},"2":{"en":"29 November 2025","hi":"29 नवंबर 2025"},"3":{"en":"30 November 2025","hi":"30 नवंबर 2025"},"4":{"en":"1 December 2025","hi":"1 दिसंबर 2025"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 30 November 2025</b><br>The <b>Syed Modi India International 2025</b>, a <b>BWF World Tour Super 300</b> event held at Lucknow, concluded on <b>30 November 2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The tournament is named after <b>Syed Modi</b>, the Indian badminton player and Arjuna awardee, and is held annually at the Babu Banarasi Das Indoor Stadium in Lucknow.<br>• It forms part of the <b>BWF World Tour</b>, whose tiers are Super 1000, Super 750, Super 500, Super 300 and Super 100.<br>• Indian shuttlers such as <b>P.V. Sindhu, Kidambi Srikanth and Lakshya Sen</b> have won titles at this event.<br>• Other major Indian badminton events are the <b>India Open (Super 750)</b> and the Odisha Open.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the 2025 Syed Modi India International ended on 30 November 2025.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 30 नवंबर 2025</b><br><b>BWF विश्व टूर सुपर 300</b> श्रेणी का <b>सैयद मोदी इंडिया इंटरनेशनल 2025</b>, जो लखनऊ में हुआ, <b>30 नवंबर 2025</b> को समाप्त हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह टूर्नामेंट भारतीय बैडमिंटन खिलाड़ी तथा अर्जुन पुरस्कार विजेता <b>सैयद मोदी</b> के नाम पर है और प्रतिवर्ष लखनऊ के बाबू बनारसी दास इंडोर स्टेडियम में होता है।<br>• यह <b>BWF विश्व टूर</b> का भाग है, जिसके स्तर सुपर 1000, सुपर 750, सुपर 500, सुपर 300 तथा सुपर 100 हैं।<br>• <b>पी. वी. सिंधु, किदांबी श्रीकांत तथा लक्ष्य सेन</b> जैसे भारतीय खिलाड़ी इस प्रतियोगिता में खिताब जीत चुके हैं।<br>• भारत की अन्य प्रमुख बैडमिंटन प्रतियोगिताएँ <b>इंडिया ओपन (सुपर 750)</b> तथा ओडिशा ओपन हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि सैयद मोदी इंडिया इंटरनेशनल 2025, 30 नवंबर 2025 को समाप्त हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072723","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which country was the 2025 Badminton World Federation (BWF) World Tour Finals, featuring leading badminton players including Indian participants, held? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2025 BWF विश्व टूर फाइनल्स, जिसमें भारतीय खिलाड़ियों सहित प्रमुख बैडमिंटन खिलाड़ियों ने भाग लिया, किस देश में आयोजित हुआ? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"China","hi":"चीन"},"2":{"en":"Malaysia","hi":"मलेशिया"},"3":{"en":"Thailand","hi":"थाईलैंड"},"4":{"en":"Indonesia","hi":"इंडोनेशिया"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – China</b><br>The <b>2025 BWF World Tour Finals</b> were held in <b>China</b>, at the Hangzhou Olympic Sports Centre, continuing the event's tradition of being staged in Chinese cities in recent years.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The BWF World Tour Finals is the season-ending tournament for the <b>top eight players or pairs</b> in the World Tour rankings.<br>• It was first held in 2018 and has been hosted in Guangzhou, Bangkok and Hangzhou in different years.<br>• Indian participants in recent editions have included <b>P.V. Sindhu, Lakshya Sen, Satwiksairaj Rankireddy and Chirag Shetty</b>.<br>• <b>Malaysia, Thailand and Indonesia</b> host other BWF World Tour events, including the Malaysia Open, Thailand Open and Indonesia Open.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the 2025 BWF World Tour Finals were held in China.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – चीन</b><br><b>2025 BWF विश्व टूर फाइनल्स</b> <b>चीन</b> में हांगझोऊ ओलंपिक स्पोर्ट्स सेंटर में आयोजित हुआ, जिससे हाल के वर्षों में इस आयोजन के चीनी नगरों में होने की परंपरा जारी रही।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BWF विश्व टूर फाइनल्स विश्व टूर रैंकिंग के <b>शीर्ष आठ खिलाड़ियों या युगलों</b> की मौसम-समापन प्रतियोगिता है।<br>• यह पहली बार 2018 में हुई और विभिन्न वर्षों में ग्वांगझोऊ, बैंकॉक तथा हांगझोऊ में आयोजित हुई।<br>• हाल के संस्करणों में भारतीय प्रतिभागियों में <b>पी. वी. सिंधु, लक्ष्य सेन, सात्विकसाईराज रंकीरेड्डी तथा चिराग शेट्टी</b> सम्मिलित रहे।<br>• <b>मलेशिया, थाईलैंड तथा इंडोनेशिया</b> अन्य BWF विश्व टूर आयोजनों की मेजबानी करते हैं, जैसे मलेशिया ओपन, थाईलैंड ओपन तथा इंडोनेशिया ओपन।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि 2025 BWF विश्व टूर फाइनल्स चीन में हुए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072724","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"What was the primary expected outcome of abolishing import licensing requirements under India’s economic reforms? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के आर्थिक सुधारों के अंतर्गत आयात लाइसेंसिंग की आवश्यकताओं को समाप्त करने का प्राथमिक अपेक्षित परिणाम क्या था? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increased efficiency and competition","hi":"दक्षता तथा प्रतिस्पर्धा में वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"Complete elimination of imports and foreign goods","hi":"आयात तथा विदेशी वस्तुओं का पूर्ण उन्मूलन"},"3":{"en":"Increased government control and regulation over trade","hi":"व्यापार पर सरकारी नियंत्रण एवं नियमन में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Restriction of foreign competition and market access","hi":"विदेशी प्रतिस्पर्धा तथा बाजार पहुँच का प्रतिबंध"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Increased efficiency and competition</b><br>Abolishing <b>import licensing</b> in the 1991 reforms was expected to <b>increase efficiency and competition</b> by allowing imports of capital goods and inputs, exposing Indian industry to global competition and lowering costs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Import licensing was abolished for most items in the <b>1990s</b>, and quantitative restrictions were removed by <b>2000-01</b>, except for some consumer goods.<br>• The reforms also involved <b>tariff reduction, rupee devaluation, removal of industrial licensing and opening to foreign direct investment</b>.<br>• The <b>Export-Import Policy of 1992</b> and later the Foreign Trade Policy replaced licensing with a negative list approach.<br>• The reforms did not eliminate imports or restrict competition; they reduced government control over trade.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because removing import licensing aimed at efficiency and competition.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – दक्षता तथा प्रतिस्पर्धा में वृद्धि</b><br>1991 के सुधारों में <b>आयात लाइसेंसिंग</b> समाप्त करने से अपेक्षा थी कि पूँजीगत वस्तुओं तथा कच्चे माल के आयात की अनुमति मिलने से <b>दक्षता तथा प्रतिस्पर्धा बढ़ेगी</b>, भारतीय उद्योग वैश्विक प्रतिस्पर्धा के सामने आएगा और लागत घटेगी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अधिकांश वस्तुओं पर आयात लाइसेंसिंग <b>1990 के दशक</b> में समाप्त हुई, और कुछ उपभोक्ता वस्तुओं के अतिरिक्त मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंध <b>2000-01</b> तक हटा दिए गए।<br>• सुधारों में <b>सीमा शुल्क में कमी, रुपये का अवमूल्यन, औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग की समाप्ति तथा प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश के लिए द्वार खोलना</b> भी सम्मिलित था।<br>• <b>1992 की निर्यात-आयात नीति</b> तथा बाद की विदेश व्यापार नीति ने लाइसेंसिंग के स्थान पर नकारात्मक सूची दृष्टिकोण अपनाया।<br>• सुधारों ने आयात समाप्त नहीं किए और न प्रतिस्पर्धा रोकी; उन्होंने व्यापार पर सरकारी नियंत्रण घटाया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि आयात लाइसेंसिंग हटाने का उद्देश्य दक्षता एवं प्रतिस्पर्धा था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072725","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Ease of Doing Business (EoDB) reforms seek to enhance India’s attractiveness as an investment destination for which of the following? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यवसाय सुगमता (EoDB) सुधार निम्नलिखित में से किसके लिए भारत की निवेश-गंतव्य के रूप में आकर्षकता बढ़ाना चाहते हैं? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Domestic investors while excluding foreign investors","hi":"घरेलू निवेशक, विदेशी निवेशकों को छोड़कर"},"2":{"en":"Foreign investors while excluding domestic investors","hi":"विदेशी निवेशक, घरेलू निवेशकों को छोड़कर"},"3":{"en":"Both domestic and foreign investors","hi":"घरेलू तथा विदेशी दोनों निवेशक"},"4":{"en":"Government agencies rather than private investors","hi":"निजी निवेशकों के स्थान पर सरकारी एजेंसियाँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both domestic and foreign investors</b><br><b>Ease of Doing Business</b> reforms aim to improve India's investment climate for <b>both domestic and foreign investors</b>, by simplifying procedures, reducing compliance costs and making regulations transparent and predictable.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Reforms include <b>single window clearance, online approvals, decriminalisation of minor offences, insolvency and labour law reform, and the National Logistics Policy</b>.<br>• India's improvement in the old World Bank EoDB ranking was driven by reforms in <b>starting a business, paying taxes, trading across borders and resolving insolvency</b>.<br>• A better business environment benefits <b>MSMEs and start-ups</b> along with large investors, and a level playing field is central to the reforms.<br>• Excluding either domestic or foreign investors, or favouring government agencies, would defeat the purpose of the reforms.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because EoDB reforms aim to attract both domestic and foreign investors.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – घरेलू तथा विदेशी दोनों निवेशक</b><br><b>व्यवसाय सुगमता</b> सुधार प्रक्रियाएँ सरल करके, अनुपालन लागत घटाकर तथा नियमों को पारदर्शी एवं पूर्वानुमेय बनाकर <b>घरेलू तथा विदेशी दोनों निवेशकों</b> के लिए भारत का निवेश वातावरण सुधारना चाहते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सुधारों में <b>एकल खिड़की मंजूरी, ऑनलाइन अनुमोदन, छोटे अपराधों का अपराधीकरण घटाना, दिवाला एवं श्रम विधि सुधार तथा राष्ट्रीय लॉजिस्टिक्स नीति</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• विश्व बैंक के पुराने EoDB सूचकांक में भारत का सुधार <b>व्यवसाय प्रारंभ करने, कर भरने, सीमा पार व्यापार तथा दिवाला निपटान</b> के सुधारों से हुआ।<br>• बेहतर व्यावसायिक वातावरण से बड़े निवेशकों के साथ <b>MSME तथा स्टार्ट-अप</b> को भी लाभ होता है, और समान अवसर का क्षेत्र इन सुधारों का केंद्र है।<br>• घरेलू या विदेशी निवेशकों में से किसी को बाहर रखना, या सरकारी एजेंसियों को वरीयता देना सुधारों के उद्देश्य को विफल कर देगा।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि EoDB सुधार घरेलू तथा विदेशी दोनों निवेशकों को आकर्षित करना चाहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072726","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Following the economic reforms introduced in India in 1991, which production shift was encouraged by export-oriented agricultural policies? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 में भारत में लाए गए आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद निर्यात-उन्मुख कृषि नीतियों द्वारा उत्पादन में कौन-सा बदलाव प्रोत्साहित किया गया? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"From horticultural crops to pulses","hi":"बागवानी फसलों से दलहन की ओर"},"2":{"en":"From pulses to horticultural crops","hi":"दलहन से बागवानी फसलों की ओर"},"3":{"en":"From food grains to cash crops","hi":"खाद्यान्न से नकदी फसलों की ओर"},"4":{"en":"From cash crops to food grains","hi":"नकदी फसलों से खाद्यान्न की ओर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – From food grains to cash crops</b><br>After the 1991 reforms, <b>export-oriented agricultural policies</b> encouraged a shift from <b>food grains to cash crops</b> such as cotton, oilseeds, sugarcane, fruits and vegetables, to take advantage of export markets.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The reforms reduced agricultural subsidies and liberalised agricultural trade, and <b>devaluation of the rupee</b> made Indian farm exports more competitive.<br>• Cash crops offer higher returns but increase exposure to <b>price volatility and market risk</b>, which contributed to distress in some regions.<br>• <b>Horticulture</b> also expanded rapidly, but the broad policy-driven shift is described as food grains to cash crops.<br>• Diversification was supported by schemes such as the <b>National Horticulture Mission</b> and later the Agricultural Export Policy.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the shift encouraged was from food grains to cash crops.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – खाद्यान्न से नकदी फसलों की ओर</b><br>1991 के सुधारों के बाद <b>निर्यात-उन्मुख कृषि नीतियों</b> ने निर्यात बाजारों का लाभ उठाने हेतु <b>खाद्यान्न से नकदी फसलों</b> जैसे कपास, तिलहन, गन्ना, फल एवं सब्जियों की ओर बदलाव को प्रोत्साहित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सुधारों ने कृषि सब्सिडी घटाई तथा कृषि व्यापार का उदारीकरण किया, और <b>रुपये के अवमूल्यन</b> ने भारतीय कृषि निर्यात को अधिक प्रतिस्पर्धी बनाया।<br>• नकदी फसलें अधिक प्रतिफल देती हैं, परंतु <b>मूल्य अस्थिरता तथा बाजार जोखिम</b> बढ़ाती हैं, जिससे कुछ क्षेत्रों में संकट बढ़ा।<br>• <b>बागवानी</b> का भी तेज विस्तार हुआ, परंतु नीति-प्रेरित व्यापक बदलाव खाद्यान्न से नकदी फसलों की ओर माना जाता है।<br>• विविधीकरण को <b>राष्ट्रीय बागवानी मिशन</b> तथा बाद की कृषि निर्यात नीति जैसी योजनाओं का सहारा मिला।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि प्रोत्साहित बदलाव खाद्यान्न से नकदी फसलों की ओर था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072727","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"A solid disc and a ring are released simultaneously from rest at the same height on the same inclined plane. Both objects roll without slipping. Which of the following reaches the bottom of the incline first? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक ठोस चकती तथा एक वलय को एक ही आनत तल पर समान ऊँचाई से एक साथ विराम से छोड़ा जाता है। दोनों बिना फिसले लुढ़कते हैं। निम्नलिखित में से कौन आनत तल के तल पर पहले पहुँचेगा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The ring","hi":"वलय"},"2":{"en":"The solid disc","hi":"ठोस चकती"},"3":{"en":"The solid disc and the ring simultaneously","hi":"ठोस चकती तथा वलय एक साथ"},"4":{"en":"The solid disc or the ring, depending on their masses","hi":"द्रव्यमान के आधार पर ठोस चकती या वलय"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The solid disc</b><br>For rolling without slipping, the acceleration down the incline is \\(a = \\frac{g \\sin\\theta}{1 + k^2/R^2}\\), which is larger for a smaller moment of inertia; the <b>solid disc</b> has \\(k^2/R^2 = 1/2\\) while the <b>ring</b> has 1, so the <b>disc reaches the bottom first</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The result is <b>independent of mass and radius</b>, depending only on the distribution of mass (radius of gyration).<br>• Order of arrival for rolling bodies is <b>sphere, disc, hollow sphere, ring</b> from fastest to slowest.<br>• Rolling friction is negligible here, and the loss of potential energy appears as both translational and rotational kinetic energy.<br>• The ring's larger moment of inertia means more energy goes into rotation and less into forward motion.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the solid disc reaches the bottom first.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ठोस चकती</b><br>बिना फिसले लुढ़कने पर आनत तल पर त्वरण \\(a = \\frac{g \\sin\\theta}{1 + k^2/R^2}\\) होता है, जो जड़त्व आघूर्ण के छोटे होने पर अधिक होता है; <b>ठोस चकती</b> में \\(k^2/R^2 = 1/2\\) तथा <b>वलय</b> में 1 होता है, इसलिए <b>चकती पहले तल पर पहुँचती है</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह परिणाम <b>द्रव्यमान तथा त्रिज्या पर निर्भर नहीं</b> करता, बल्कि केवल द्रव्यमान वितरण (परिभ्रमण त्रिज्या) पर निर्भर है।<br>• लुढ़कते पिंडों के पहुँचने का क्रम तेज से धीमे – <b>गोला, चकती, खोखला गोला, वलय</b> है।<br>• यहाँ लोटन घर्षण नगण्य है, और स्थितिज ऊर्जा की हानि स्थानांतरणीय तथा घूर्णीय गतिज ऊर्जा दोनों में प्रकट होती है।<br>• वलय का अधिक जड़त्व आघूर्ण होने से अधिक ऊर्जा घूर्णन में जाती है और अग्रगति में कम।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि ठोस चकती पहले तल पर पहुँचती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072728","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Which of the following strategies is the most ecologically sustainable for long-term water-resource management? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दीर्घकालिक जल-संसाधन प्रबंधन हेतु निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी रणनीति पारिस्थितिक रूप से सर्वाधिक संपोषणीय है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mega-dam construction, river diversion, and centralised water storage.","hi":"महा-बाँध निर्माण, नदी परिवर्तन तथा केंद्रीकृत जल भंडारण।"},"2":{"en":"Groundwater extraction, deep-well expansion, and emergency pumping.","hi":"भूजल निष्कर्षण, गहरे कुओं का विस्तार तथा आपातकालीन पंपिंग।"},"3":{"en":"Rainwater harvesting, afforestation, and local catchment management.","hi":"वर्षा जल संचयन, वनीकरण तथा स्थानीय जलग्रहण प्रबंधन।"},"4":{"en":"Canal expansion, cash-crop irrigation, and increased water diversion.","hi":"नहर विस्तार, नकदी फसल सिंचाई तथा जल परिवर्तन में वृद्धि।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Rainwater harvesting, afforestation, and local catchment management.</b><br><b>Rainwater harvesting, afforestation and local catchment management</b> are the most ecologically sustainable strategies, because they <b>recharge groundwater, reduce run-off, restore the local water cycle</b> and use decentralised, low-impact methods.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• These approaches follow the principle of <b>demand-side management and decentralised conservation</b>, and are the basis of the government's <b>Jal Shakti Abhiyan and the Catch the Rain campaign</b>.<br>• Mega-dams and river diversion cause <b>displacement, siltation and loss of river ecology</b>, and deep-well extraction depletes aquifers irreversibly.<br>• Afforestation improves <b>soil infiltration and reduces soil erosion</b>, and watershed development raises the water table.<br>• Canal expansion for cash crops increases <b>waterlogging, salinity and inequity</b> in water use.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because rainwater harvesting, afforestation and catchment management are the most sustainable.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वर्षा जल संचयन, वनीकरण तथा स्थानीय जलग्रहण प्रबंधन।</b><br><b>वर्षा जल संचयन, वनीकरण तथा स्थानीय जलग्रहण प्रबंधन</b> पारिस्थितिक रूप से सर्वाधिक संपोषणीय रणनीतियाँ हैं, क्योंकि ये <b>भूजल का पुनर्भरण करती हैं, अपवाह घटाती हैं, स्थानीय जल-चक्र को पुनर्जीवित करती हैं</b> तथा विकेंद्रीकृत, अल्प-प्रभाव वाली विधियाँ अपनाती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ये उपाय <b>माँग-पक्ष प्रबंधन तथा विकेंद्रीकृत संरक्षण</b> के सिद्धांत पर आधारित हैं और सरकार के <b>जल शक्ति अभियान तथा कैच द रेन अभियान</b> का आधार हैं।<br>• महा-बाँध तथा नदी परिवर्तन से <b>विस्थापन, तलछट भराव तथा नदी पारिस्थितिकी की हानि</b> होती है, और गहरे कुओं से भूजल स्तर अपरिवर्तनीय रूप से गिरता है।<br>• वनीकरण <b>मृदा अंतःस्रवण बढ़ाता तथा मृदा अपरदन घटाता</b> है, और जलग्रहण विकास से भूजल स्तर ऊपर आता है।<br>• नकदी फसलों हेतु नहर विस्तार से <b>जलभराव, लवणता तथा जल-उपयोग में असमानता</b> बढ़ती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि वर्षा जल संचयन, वनीकरण तथा जलग्रहण प्रबंधन सर्वाधिक संपोषणीय हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072729","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following situations most clearly demonstrates environmental injustice? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी स्थिति पर्यावरणीय अन्याय (environmental injustice) को सर्वाधिक स्पष्ट रूप से दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Urban communities depending on rivers while receiving adequate water supplies","hi":"नदियों पर निर्भर शहरी समुदायों को पर्याप्त जल आपूर्ति मिलना"},"2":{"en":"Tribal communities disproportionately displaced by dams despite limited benefits","hi":"बाँधों से असमान रूप से विस्थापित जनजातीय समुदाय, जिन्हें सीमित लाभ मिले"},"3":{"en":"Increased hydropower generation in industrial regions","hi":"औद्योगिक क्षेत्रों में जलविद्युत उत्पादन में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Farming communities adopting drip irrigation to conserve water","hi":"जल संरक्षण हेतु ड्रिप सिंचाई अपनाने वाले कृषक समुदाय"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Tribal communities disproportionately displaced by dams despite limited benefits</b><br><b>Environmental injustice</b> occurs when the costs of environmental projects fall <b>disproportionately on poor and marginalised communities</b> who receive few benefits; the <b>displacement of tribal communities by dams</b> with limited benefit to them is the clearest example.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Environmental justice links <b>environmental protection with social equity, human rights and fair distribution of costs and benefits</b>.<br>• In India, displacement by large dams has affected <b>adivasi communities</b> far more than their share of the population, a point raised by the Narmada Bachao Andolan.<br>• Other examples include <b>pollution in low-income neighbourhoods, landfills near slums and loss of forest rights</b> under the Forest Rights Act.<br>• Adequate water supply to urban communities and adoption of drip irrigation are examples of equity, not injustice.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because disproportionate tribal displacement by dams shows environmental injustice.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाँधों से असमान रूप से विस्थापित जनजातीय समुदाय, जिन्हें सीमित लाभ मिले</b><br><b>पर्यावरणीय अन्याय</b> तब होता है जब पर्यावरणीय परियोजनाओं की लागत <b>गरीब तथा हाशिये के समुदायों पर असमान रूप से</b> पड़ती है जिन्हें लाभ कम मिलता है; <b>बाँधों से जनजातीय समुदायों का विस्थापन</b> और उन्हें सीमित लाभ मिलना इसका स्पष्टतम उदाहरण है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पर्यावरणीय न्याय <b>पर्यावरण संरक्षण को सामाजिक समता, मानव अधिकार तथा लागत-लाभ के न्यायपूर्ण वितरण</b> से जोड़ता है।<br>• भारत में बड़े बाँधों से विस्थापन ने जनसंख्या में उनके हिस्से की तुलना में <b>आदिवासी समुदायों</b> को अधिक प्रभावित किया, जिसे नर्मदा बचाओ आंदोलन ने उठाया।<br>• अन्य उदाहरणों में <b>निम्न-आय क्षेत्रों में प्रदूषण, झुग्गियों के निकट कचरा भराव क्षेत्र तथा वन अधिकार अधिनियम के अंतर्गत वन अधिकारों की हानि</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• शहरी समुदायों को पर्याप्त जल आपूर्ति तथा ड्रिप सिंचाई अपनाना समता के उदाहरण हैं, अन्याय के नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि बाँधों से असमान जनजातीय विस्थापन पर्यावरणीय अन्याय दर्शाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072730","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"A leftward shift in the demand curve of a commodity indicates: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी वस्तु की माँग वक्र में बाईं ओर खिसकाव क्या दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Decrease in quantity demanded","hi":"माँगी गई मात्रा में कमी"},"2":{"en":"Increase in demand","hi":"माँग में वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"Decrease in demand","hi":"माँग में कमी"},"4":{"en":"Increase in quantity demanded","hi":"माँगी गई मात्रा में वृद्धि"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Decrease in demand</b><br>A <b>leftward shift of the demand curve</b> indicates a <b>decrease in demand</b> at every price, caused by factors other than the good's own price, such as a fall in income, a rise in the price of a substitute or a change in tastes.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>movement along the demand curve</b> is a change in quantity demanded due to a change in the <b>good's own price</b>.<br>• A <b>rightward shift</b> means an increase in demand, and a leftward shift means a decrease.<br>• Determinants of demand other than price include <b>income, prices of related goods, tastes, expectations and population</b>.<br>• For normal goods, a fall in income shifts the demand curve to the left.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because a leftward shift of the demand curve shows a decrease in demand.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – माँग में कमी</b><br><b>माँग वक्र का बाईं ओर खिसकाव</b> प्रत्येक कीमत पर <b>माँग में कमी</b> दर्शाता है, जो वस्तु की अपनी कीमत के अतिरिक्त कारकों से होती है, जैसे आय में कमी, विकल्प वस्तु की कीमत में वृद्धि या रुचि में परिवर्तन।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>माँग वक्र पर गति</b> <b>वस्तु की अपनी कीमत</b> में परिवर्तन के कारण माँगी गई मात्रा में परिवर्तन है।<br>• <b>दाईं ओर खिसकाव</b> माँग में वृद्धि तथा बाईं ओर खिसकाव माँग में कमी दर्शाता है।<br>• कीमत के अतिरिक्त माँग के निर्धारक हैं – <b>आय, संबंधित वस्तुओं की कीमतें, रुचि, प्रत्याशाएँ तथा जनसंख्या</b>।<br>• सामान्य वस्तुओं में आय घटने पर माँग वक्र बाईं ओर खिसक जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि माँग वक्र का बाईं ओर खिसकाव माँग में कमी दर्शाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072731","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon below to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the total number of households represented in this data?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर देने के लिए नीचे दिए गए बारंबारता बहुभुज को देखिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>इस आँकड़े में दर्शाए गए परिवारों की कुल संख्या क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100"},"2":{"en":"105"},"3":{"en":"110"},"4":{"en":"115"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Reading the polygon: 0–20 → 12, 20–40 → 28, 40–60 → 35, 60–80 → 20, 80–100 → 10<br>Total = \\(12 + 28 + 35 + 20 + 10\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{105}\\) households<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 105.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज से पढ़ने पर: 0–20 → 12, 20–40 → 28, 40–60 → 35, 60–80 → 20, 80–100 → 10<br>कुल = \\(12 + 28 + 35 + 20 + 10\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{105}\\) परिवार<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 105 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q51.jpg"]}},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072732","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"The product of two decimals is 0.768. If one of the numbers is 1.6, find the other number. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो दशमलव संख्याओं का गुणनफल 0.768 है। यदि उनमें से एक संख्या 1.6 है, तो दूसरी संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.35"},"2":{"en":"0.78"},"3":{"en":"0.45"},"4":{"en":"0.48"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Other number \\(= \\frac{0.768}{1.6}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{768}{1600} = \\boxed{0.48}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 0.48.</b>","hi":"दूसरी संख्या \\(= \\frac{0.768}{1.6}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{768}{1600} = \\boxed{0.48}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 0.48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072733","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A vehicle has a running speed of 88 km/h, but due to frequent halts, its average speed reduces to 66 km/h. Find the time it stops in one hour. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वाहन की चलने की चाल 88 km/घंटा है, परंतु बार-बार रुकने के कारण उसकी औसत चाल 66 km/घंटा हो जाती है। एक घंटे में उसके रुकने का समय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 minutes","hi":"8 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"10 minutes","hi":"10 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"12 minutes","hi":"12 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"15 minutes","hi":"15 मिनट"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Stoppage time per hour \\(= 60\\left(1 - \\frac{66}{88}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= 60 \\times \\frac{22}{88} = 60 \\times \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{15}\\) minutes<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 15 minutes.</b>","hi":"प्रति घंटा रुकने का समय \\(= 60\\left(1 - \\frac{66}{88}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= 60 \\times \\frac{22}{88} = 60 \\times \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{15}\\) मिनट<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 15 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072734","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\frac{(0.98)^3-(0.02)^3}{0.9604+0.0196+0.0004}\\). [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\frac{(0.98)^3-(0.02)^3}{0.9604+0.0196+0.0004}\\) [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.24"},"2":{"en":"0.45"},"3":{"en":"0.66"},"4":{"en":"0.96"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Using \\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\\) with \\(a = 0.98\\), \\(b = 0.02\\)<br>\\(a^2 + ab + b^2 = 0.9604 + 0.0196 + 0.0004\\), which cancels with the denominator<br>Value \\(= a - b = 0.98 - 0.02 = \\boxed{0.96}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 0.96.</b>","hi":"\\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\\) का प्रयोग, जहाँ \\(a = 0.98\\), \\(b = 0.02\\)<br>\\(a^2 + ab + b^2 = 0.9604 + 0.0196 + 0.0004\\), जो हर से कट जाता है<br>मान \\(= a - b = 0.98 - 0.02 = \\boxed{0.96}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 0.96 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072735","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If the 6-digit number 15x1y2 is divisible by 44, then find the value of (x + y). [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 6 अंकों की संख्या 15x1y2, 44 से विभाज्य है, तो (x + y) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"7"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"44 = 4 × 11. Divisibility by 4 needs \\(y2\\) divisible by 4, so y is odd<br>Divisibility by 11: \\((1 + x + y) - (5 + 1 + 2) = x + y - 7\\) must be 0 (or a multiple of 11)<br>With y odd, \\(x + y = 7\\) works (e.g. x = 2, y = 5)<br>\\(x + y = \\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 7.</b>","hi":"44 = 4 × 11. 4 से विभाज्यता के लिए \\(y2\\), 4 से विभाज्य होना चाहिए, अतः y विषम है<br>11 से विभाज्यता: \\((1 + x + y) - (5 + 1 + 2) = x + y - 7\\) शून्य (या 11 का गुणज) होना चाहिए<br>y विषम होने पर \\(x + y = 7\\) संभव है (जैसे x = 2, y = 5)<br>\\(x + y = \\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072736","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B are partners in a business. A contributes 1/3 of the capital for 9 months and B receives 2/5 of the total profit. For how long was B's money used in the business? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A और B एक व्यवसाय में साझेदार हैं। A पूँजी का 1/3 भाग 9 महीनों के लिए लगाता है और B कुल लाभ का 2/5 भाग प्राप्त करता है। B का धन कितने समय तक व्यवसाय में लगा रहा? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 months","hi":"4 महीने"},"2":{"en":"6 months","hi":"6 महीने"},"3":{"en":"3 months","hi":"3 महीने"},"4":{"en":"5 months","hi":"5 महीने"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Profit ratio A : B \\(= \\frac{3}{5} : \\frac{2}{5} = 3 : 2\\)<br>A's capital × time \\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 9 = 3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3}{\\frac{2}{3} \\times t} = \\frac{3}{2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2t}{3} = 2\\)<br>\\(t = \\boxed{3}\\) months<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3 months.</b>","hi":"लाभ अनुपात A : B \\(= \\frac{3}{5} : \\frac{2}{5} = 3 : 2\\)<br>A की पूँजी × समय \\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 9 = 3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3}{\\frac{2}{3} \\times t} = \\frac{3}{2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2t}{3} = 2\\)<br>\\(t = \\boxed{3}\\) महीने<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 महीने है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072737","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average weight of 8 persons increases by 2.5 kg when a new person comes in place of one of them weighing 65 kg. What is the weight of the new person? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जब 65 kg वजन वाले एक व्यक्ति के स्थान पर एक नया व्यक्ति आता है, तो 8 व्यक्तियों का औसत वजन 2.5 kg बढ़ जाता है। नए व्यक्ति का वजन क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75 kg"},"2":{"en":"85 kg"},"3":{"en":"65 kg"},"4":{"en":"45 kg"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Total increase \\(= 8 \\times 2.5 = 20\\) kg<br>Weight of the new person \\(= 65 + 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{85}\\) kg<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 85 kg.</b>","hi":"कुल वृद्धि \\(= 8 \\times 2.5 = 20\\) kg<br>नए व्यक्ति का वजन \\(= 65 + 20\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{85}\\) kg<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 85 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072738","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"A line cuts the x-axis at A and the y-axis at B. If the midpoint of AB is (3, −2), what is the equation of the line? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक रेखा x-अक्ष को A पर और y-अक्ष को B पर काटती है। यदि AB का मध्य-बिंदु (3, −2) है, तो रेखा का समीकरण क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2x − 3y = 12"},"2":{"en":"3x − 2y = 6"},"3":{"en":"2x + 3y = 12"},"4":{"en":"3x + 2y = 6"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let A = (a, 0) and B = (0, b). Midpoint: \\(\\left(\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{b}{2}\\right) = (3, -2)\\)<br>\\(a = 6\\), \\(b = -4\\)<br>Intercept form: \\(\\frac{x}{6} + \\frac{y}{-4} = 1 \\Rightarrow 2x - 3y = 12\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{2x - 3y = 12}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2x − 3y = 12.</b>","hi":"A = (a, 0) और B = (0, b) मानिए। मध्य-बिंदु: \\(\\left(\\frac{a}{2}, \\frac{b}{2}\\right) = (3, -2)\\)<br>\\(a = 6\\), \\(b = -4\\)<br>अंतःखंड रूप: \\(\\frac{x}{6} + \\frac{y}{-4} = 1 \\Rightarrow 2x - 3y = 12\\)<br>अतः \\(\\boxed{2x - 3y = 12}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2x − 3y = 12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072739","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cube with a diagonal of 20√3 cm is melted into a cuboid. If the length of the cuboid is equal to the side of the cube and the breadth is 10 cm, find its height. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"20√3 cm विकर्ण वाले एक घन को पिघलाकर एक घनाभ बनाया जाता है। यदि घनाभ की लंबाई घन की भुजा के बराबर है और चौड़ाई 10 cm है, तो उसकी ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 cm"},"2":{"en":"16 cm"},"3":{"en":"28 cm"},"4":{"en":"40 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"234\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 234 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L147 186M26 186L26 65M147 186L208 147M147 186L147 65M26 65L147 65M26 65L87 26M208 147L208 26M147 65L208 26M87 26L208 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 186L87 147M87 147L208 147M87 147L87 26M26 186L208 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"87\" y=\"202\">a</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"182\">a</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"129\">a</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"99\">20√3</text></g></svg><br>Diagonal \\(= a\\sqrt{3} = 20\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow a = 20\\) cm<br>Volume \\(= 20^3 = 8000\\) cm³<br>\\(20 \\times 10 \\times h = 8000 \\Rightarrow 200h = 8000\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{40}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 40 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"234\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 234 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L147 186M26 186L26 65M147 186L208 147M147 186L147 65M26 65L147 65M26 65L87 26M208 147L208 26M147 65L208 26M87 26L208 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 186L87 147M87 147L208 147M87 147L87 26M26 186L208 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"87\" y=\"202\">a</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"182\">a</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"129\">a</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"99\">20√3</text></g></svg><br>विकर्ण \\(= a\\sqrt{3} = 20\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow a = 20\\) cm<br>आयतन \\(= 20^3 = 8000\\) cm³<br>\\(20 \\times 10 \\times h = 8000 \\Rightarrow 200h = 8000\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{40}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 40 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072740","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A fan rotates at 120π radians per second. Find the number of revolutions in one minute. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पंखा 120π रेडियन प्रति सेकंड की गति से घूमता है। एक मिनट में चक्करों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3000"},"2":{"en":"3200"},"3":{"en":"3800"},"4":{"en":"3600"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Revolutions per second \\(= \\frac{120\\pi}{2\\pi} = 60\\)<br>Revolutions per minute \\(= 60 \\times 60\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3600.</b>","hi":"प्रति सेकंड चक्कर \\(= \\frac{120\\pi}{2\\pi} = 60\\)<br>प्रति मिनट चक्कर \\(= 60 \\times 60\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072741","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If secθ = 13/12 and θ is an acute angle, find the value of cosecθ − cotθ. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि secθ = 13/12 है और θ एक न्यून कोण है, तो cosecθ − cotθ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{12}{5}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{13}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{12}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{12}{13}\\), so \\(\\sin\\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{144}{169}} = \\frac{5}{13}\\)<br>\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta - \\cot\\theta = \\frac{13}{5} - \\frac{12}{5} = \\frac{1}{5}\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{12}{13}\\), अतः \\(\\sin\\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{144}{169}} = \\frac{5}{13}\\)<br>\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta - \\cot\\theta = \\frac{13}{5} - \\frac{12}{5} = \\frac{1}{5}\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072742","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\sqrt{11 - 2\\sqrt{30}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11 - 2\\sqrt{30}}}\\). [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{11 - 2\\sqrt{30}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11 - 2\\sqrt{30}}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{5}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{6}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{6}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Formula:</b> \\(\\sqrt{a + b - 2\\sqrt{ab}} = \\sqrt{a} - \\sqrt{b}\\) (where \\(a > b\\))<br><br><b>Step 1:</b> Split 11 into two numbers whose product is 30: \\(11 = 6 + 5\\) and \\(6 \\times 5 = 30\\)<br>\\(11 - 2\\sqrt{30} = 6 + 5 - 2\\sqrt{6 \\times 5} = (\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5})^2\\)<br>So, \\(\\sqrt{11 - 2\\sqrt{30}} = \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}\\)<br><br><b>Step 2:</b> Find the reciprocal by rationalising<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5}}{(\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5})} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5}}{6 - 5} = \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5}\\)<br><br><b>Step 3:</b> Put the values in the expression<br>\\((\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}) - (\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5})\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}\\)<br>\\(= -2\\sqrt{5}\\)<br><br><b>Quick check:</b> \\(\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5} \\approx 0.213\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{0.213} \\approx 4.69\\), so \\(0.213 - 4.69 \\approx -4.47 = -2\\sqrt{5}\\) ✓<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{5}\\).</b>","hi":"<b>सूत्र:</b> \\(\\sqrt{a + b - 2\\sqrt{ab}} = \\sqrt{a} - \\sqrt{b}\\) (जहाँ \\(a > b\\))<br><br><b>चरण 1:</b> 11 को ऐसी दो संख्याओं के योग में तोड़िए जिनका गुणनफल 30 हो: \\(11 = 6 + 5\\) और \\(6 \\times 5 = 30\\)<br>\\(11 - 2\\sqrt{30} = 6 + 5 - 2\\sqrt{6 \\times 5} = (\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5})^2\\)<br>अतः \\(\\sqrt{11 - 2\\sqrt{30}} = \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}\\)<br><br><b>चरण 2:</b> परिमेयकरण द्वारा व्युत्क्रम ज्ञात कीजिए<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5}}{(\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5})(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5})} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5}}{6 - 5} = \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5}\\)<br><br><b>चरण 3:</b> व्यंजक में मान रखिए<br>\\((\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}) - (\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{5})\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5}\\)<br>\\(= -2\\sqrt{5}\\)<br><br><b>जाँच:</b> \\(\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{5} \\approx 0.213\\) और \\(\\frac{1}{0.213} \\approx 4.69\\), इसलिए \\(0.213 - 4.69 \\approx -4.47 = -2\\sqrt{5}\\) ✓<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072743","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"Tea worth ₹120 per kg and ₹140 per kg are mixed with a third variety in the ratio 1 : 1 : 2. If the mixture costs ₹150 per kg, find the price per kg of the third variety. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹120 प्रति kg और ₹140 प्रति kg मूल्य की चाय को 1 : 1 : 2 के अनुपात में तीसरी किस्म के साथ मिलाया जाता है। यदि मिश्रण का मूल्य ₹150 प्रति kg है, तो तीसरी किस्म का मूल्य प्रति kg ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹135 per kg","hi":"₹135 प्रति kg"},"2":{"en":"₹150 per kg","hi":"₹150 प्रति kg"},"3":{"en":"₹185 per kg","hi":"₹185 प्रति kg"},"4":{"en":"₹170 per kg","hi":"₹170 प्रति kg"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Take 1 kg, 1 kg and 2 kg of the three varieties; total 4 kg<br>\\(\\frac{120 + 140 + 2x}{4} = 150\\)<br>\\(260 + 2x = 600 \\Rightarrow 2x = 340\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{170}\\) per kg<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹170 per kg.</b>","hi":"तीनों किस्मों के 1 kg, 1 kg और 2 kg लीजिए; कुल 4 kg<br>\\(\\frac{120 + 140 + 2x}{4} = 150\\)<br>\\(260 + 2x = 600 \\Rightarrow 2x = 340\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{170}\\) प्रति kg<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹170 प्रति kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072744","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The pie chart displays the percentage distribution of students participating in five different sports categories at a school academy. Study the following pie chart carefully to answer the question that follows.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Due to ground maintenance, the academy temporarily suspends the Basketball program. All students currently in the Basketball sector are transferred to other sports:<br>1. \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of the Basketball students are moved to Cricket.<br>2. The remaining Basketball students are moved to Badminton.<br>After this structural shift is complete, what will be the new ratio of the total number of students in Cricket to the total number of students in Badminton?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यह पाई चार्ट एक स्कूल अकादमी में पाँच विभिन्न खेल श्रेणियों में भाग लेने वाले विद्यार्थियों का प्रतिशत वितरण दर्शाता है। निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर देने के लिए पाई चार्ट को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>मैदान के रखरखाव के कारण अकादमी बास्केटबॉल कार्यक्रम को अस्थायी रूप से बंद कर देती है। बास्केटबॉल क्षेत्र के सभी विद्यार्थी अन्य खेलों में स्थानांतरित किए जाते हैं:<br>1. बास्केटबॉल के \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) विद्यार्थी क्रिकेट में जाते हैं।<br>2. शेष बास्केटबॉल विद्यार्थी बैडमिंटन में जाते हैं।<br>यह संरचनात्मक बदलाव पूरा होने के बाद, क्रिकेट में विद्यार्थियों की कुल संख्या और बैडमिंटन में विद्यार्थियों की कुल संख्या का नया अनुपात क्या होगा?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7:8"},"2":{"en":"8:5"},"3":{"en":"4:9"},"4":{"en":"9:7"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Cricket 30%, Football 25%, Badminton 20%, Basketball 15%, Others 10%<br>Basketball students moved to Cricket \\(= \\frac{2}{3} \\times 15\\% = 10\\%\\); moved to Badminton \\(= 5\\%\\)<br>New Cricket \\(= 30\\% + 10\\% = 40\\%\\), new Badminton \\(= 20\\% + 5\\% = 25\\%\\)<br>Ratio \\(= 40 : 25 = \\boxed{8 : 5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 8:5.</b>","hi":"पाई चार्ट से: क्रिकेट 30%, फुटबॉल 25%, बैडमिंटन 20%, बास्केटबॉल 15%, अन्य 10%<br>क्रिकेट में गए बास्केटबॉल विद्यार्थी \\(= \\frac{2}{3} \\times 15\\% = 10\\%\\); बैडमिंटन में गए \\(= 5\\%\\)<br>नया क्रिकेट \\(= 30\\% + 10\\% = 40\\%\\), नया बैडमिंटन \\(= 20\\% + 5\\% = 25\\%\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= 40 : 25 = \\boxed{8 : 5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 8:5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q64.jpg"]}},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072745","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tanA = 2tanB and both A and B are acute angles, what is the value of \\(\\frac{\\tan A}{\\tan B}\\)? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि tanA = 2tanB है और A तथा B दोनों न्यून कोण हैं, तो \\(\\frac{\\tan A}{\\tan B}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan A = 2\\tan B\\)<br>Dividing both sides by \\(\\tan B\\) (non-zero as B is acute):<br>\\(\\frac{\\tan A}{\\tan B} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan A = 2\\tan B\\)<br>दोनों पक्षों को \\(\\tan B\\) से भाग देने पर (B न्यून है, अतः शून्य नहीं):<br>\\(\\frac{\\tan A}{\\tan B} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072746","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Maya does 60% of a work in 18 days. She then calls Puja and both together finish the rest of the work in 6 days. How many days would Puja alone take to complete the work? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"माया 18 दिनों में एक कार्य का 60% करती है। फिर वह पूजा को बुलाती है और दोनों मिलकर शेष कार्य 6 दिनों में पूरा करती हैं। पूजा अकेली उस कार्य को कितने दिनों में पूरा करेगी? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 days","hi":"20 दिन"},"2":{"en":"24 days","hi":"24 दिन"},"3":{"en":"25 days","hi":"25 दिन"},"4":{"en":"30 days","hi":"30 दिन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Maya alone: 60% in 18 days, so 100% in 30 days → rate \\(= \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>Together they do 40% in 6 days → rate \\(= \\frac{2}{5 \\times 6} = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>Puja's rate \\(= \\frac{1}{15} - \\frac{1}{30} = \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>Puja alone takes \\(\\boxed{30}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30 days.</b>","hi":"माया अकेली: 18 दिनों में 60%, अतः 100% 30 दिनों में → दर \\(= \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>दोनों मिलकर 6 दिनों में 40% करती हैं → दर \\(= \\frac{2}{5 \\times 6} = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>पूजा की दर \\(= \\frac{1}{15} - \\frac{1}{30} = \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>पूजा अकेली \\(\\boxed{30}\\) दिन लेगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072747","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: tan 3° · tan 15° · tan 27° · tan 39° · tan 45° · tan 51° · tan 63° · tan 75° · tan 87° [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: tan 3° · tan 15° · tan 27° · tan 39° · tan 45° · tan 51° · tan 63° · tan 75° · tan 87° [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"−1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"√3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Pair the terms: \\(\\tan 3^\\circ\\tan 87^\\circ = \\tan 3^\\circ\\cot 3^\\circ = 1\\)<br>Similarly \\(\\tan 15^\\circ\\tan 75^\\circ = 1\\), \\(\\tan 27^\\circ\\tan 63^\\circ = 1\\), \\(\\tan 39^\\circ\\tan 51^\\circ = 1\\), and \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\)<br>Product \\(= 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.</b>","hi":"पदों को जोड़े में लिखिए: \\(\\tan 3^\\circ\\tan 87^\\circ = \\tan 3^\\circ\\cot 3^\\circ = 1\\)<br>इसी प्रकार \\(\\tan 15^\\circ\\tan 75^\\circ = 1\\), \\(\\tan 27^\\circ\\tan 63^\\circ = 1\\), \\(\\tan 39^\\circ\\tan 51^\\circ = 1\\), और \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\)<br>गुणनफल \\(= 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072748","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a − b = 13 and a² − b² = 65, what is the value of 2a + 2b? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a − b = 13 और a² − b² = 65 है, तो 2a + 2b का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"26"},"2":{"en":"78"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b) = 65\\)<br>\\(13(a + b) = 65 \\Rightarrow a + b = 5\\)<br>\\(2a + 2b = 2(a + b) = \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b) = 65\\)<br>\\(13(a + b) = 65 \\Rightarrow a + b = 5\\)<br>\\(2a + 2b = 2(a + b) = \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072749","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔABC, the side lengths are AB = 10 units and BC = 12 units. The median drawn from vertex A meets the side BC at point D. The interior angle bisector of ∠B intersects the segment AD at point E. What is the ratio AE : ED? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ΔABC में, भुजाओं की लंबाई AB = 10 इकाई और BC = 12 इकाई है। शीर्ष A से खींची गई माध्यिका भुजा BC को बिंदु D पर मिलती है। ∠B का अंतः कोण समद्विभाजक खंड AD को बिंदु E पर प्रतिच्छेद करता है। AE : ED का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 : 3"},"2":{"en":"3 : 2"},"3":{"en":"4 : 3"},"4":{"en":"5 : 4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"275\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 275 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M100 26L26 196L249 196ZM100 26L137 196M26 196L123 132M52 196A26 26 0 0 0 48 182M51 180A30 30 0 0 0 38 169\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"132\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"97\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"137\" y=\"207\">D</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\">E</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"109\">10</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"11\">6</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"11\">6</text></g></svg><br>AD is a median, so \\(BD = DC = 6\\) units<br>In ΔABD, BE bisects ∠B, so by the angle bisector theorem<br>\\(\\frac{AE}{ED} = \\frac{AB}{BD} = \\frac{10}{6} = \\frac{5}{3}\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{5 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5 : 3.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"275\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 275 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M100 26L26 196L249 196ZM100 26L137 196M26 196L123 132M52 196A26 26 0 0 0 48 182M51 180A30 30 0 0 0 38 169\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"132\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"97\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"137\" y=\"207\">D</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"start\">E</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"109\">10</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"11\">6</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"11\">6</text></g></svg><br>AD माध्यिका है, अतः \\(BD = DC = 6\\) इकाई<br>ΔABD में BE, ∠B को समद्विभाजित करती है, अतः कोण समद्विभाजक प्रमेय से<br>\\(\\frac{AE}{ED} = \\frac{AB}{BD} = \\frac{10}{6} = \\frac{5}{3}\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{5 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5 : 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072750","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"A student claims that √8 + √18 = √26. Which of the following explains why the claim is incorrect? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक विद्यार्थी का दावा है कि √8 + √18 = √26। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा इस दावे के गलत होने का कारण बताता है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Square roots cannot be added.","hi":"वर्गमूलों को जोड़ा नहीं जा सकता।"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} \\ne \\sqrt{a + b}\\) in general.","hi":"सामान्यतः \\(\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} \\ne \\sqrt{a + b}\\) होता है।"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{8}\\) is rational.","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{8}\\) परिमेय है।"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{18}\\) is rational.","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{18}\\) परिमेय है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} = 5\\sqrt{2} = \\sqrt{50}\\), not \\(\\sqrt{26}\\)<br>The error is the false identity \\(\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{a + b}\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} \\ne \\sqrt{a + b}}\\) in general.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} \\ne \\sqrt{a + b}\\) in general.</b>","hi":"\\(2\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} = 5\\sqrt{2} = \\sqrt{50}\\), न कि \\(\\sqrt{26}\\)<br>त्रुटि झूठी सर्वसमिका \\(\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} = \\sqrt{a + b}\\) में है<br>अतः सामान्यतः \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} \\ne \\sqrt{a + b}}\\) होता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): सामान्यतः \\(\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} \\ne \\sqrt{a + b}\\) होता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072751","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two coplanar circles have radii r and 3r. For these circles to have exactly 3 common tangents, the distance between their centers must be: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो समतलीय वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ r और 3r हैं। इन वृत्तों की ठीक 3 उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ होने के लिए, उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी होनी चाहिए: [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2r"},"2":{"en":"3r"},"3":{"en":"4r"},"4":{"en":"5r"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Exactly three common tangents means the circles touch each other externally<br>For external contact, \\(d = R + r = 3r + r\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{4r}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4r.</b>","hi":"ठीक तीन उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ होने का अर्थ है कि वृत्त बाह्य रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं<br>बाह्य स्पर्श के लिए \\(d = R + r = 3r + r\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{4r}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4r है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072752","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"Nayana invests a total of Rs. 50,000 across five different assets, namely A, B, C, D, and E. She puts exactly 36% of the total investment amount into Asset A, and the remaining money is divided equally among the other four assets. The annualized return percentages of the different assets over a single year are illustrated in the bar graph below:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Calculate the total amount of profit Nayana makes at the end of the year across her entire portfolio.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नयना कुल रु. 50,000 को पाँच भिन्न परिसंपत्तियों A, B, C, D और E में निवेश करती है। वह कुल निवेश राशि का ठीक 36% परिसंपत्ति A में लगाती है और शेष राशि अन्य चार परिसंपत्तियों में समान रूप से बाँटती है। एक वर्ष में विभिन्न परिसंपत्तियों के वार्षिक प्रतिफल प्रतिशत नीचे दिए गए स्तंभ ग्राफ में दर्शाए गए हैं:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>वर्ष के अंत में नयना को अपने पूरे पोर्टफोलियो से प्राप्त कुल लाभ की गणना कीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 8400","hi":"रु. 8400"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 8480","hi":"रु. 8480"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 8800","hi":"रु. 8800"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 8840","hi":"रु. 8840"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Asset A \\(= 36\\% \\) of 50,000 \\(= 18{,}000\\); each of B, C, D, E \\(= \\frac{32{,}000}{4} = 8000\\)<br>Returns from the graph: A 18%, B 14%, C 28%, D 9%, E 19%<br>Profit \\(= 18{,}000 \\times \\frac{18}{100} + 8000 \\times \\frac{14 + 28 + 9 + 19}{100}\\)<br>\\(= 3240 + 8000 \\times 0.70 = 3240 + 5600\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8840}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Rs. 8840.</b>","hi":"परिसंपत्ति A \\(= 50{,}000\\) का \\(36\\% = 18{,}000\\); B, C, D, E में प्रत्येक \\(= \\frac{32{,}000}{4} = 8000\\)<br>ग्राफ से प्रतिफल: A 18%, B 14%, C 28%, D 9%, E 19%<br>लाभ \\(= 18{,}000 \\times \\frac{18}{100} + 8000 \\times \\frac{14 + 28 + 9 + 19}{100}\\)<br>\\(= 3240 + 8000 \\times 0.70 = 3240 + 5600\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8840}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): रु. 8840 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-27-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q72.jpg"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072753","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"Ria invests ₹P in Scheme A, which offers simple interest at 15% per annum for 4 years, and ₹(P + 1,680) in Scheme B, which offers compound interest at 25% per annum for 2 years, compounded annually. If the ratio of the amounts received from Scheme A and Scheme B is 4 : 5, what is the value of P? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रिया योजना A में ₹P निवेश करती है, जो 4 वर्षों के लिए 15% प्रति वर्ष साधारण ब्याज देती है, और योजना B में ₹(P + 1,680) निवेश करती है, जो 2 वर्षों के लिए 25% प्रति वर्ष वार्षिक रूप से संयोजित चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज देती है। यदि योजना A और योजना B से प्राप्त राशियों का अनुपात 4 : 5 है, तो P का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6,000"},"2":{"en":"₹5,600"},"3":{"en":"₹6,400"},"4":{"en":"₹7,200"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Scheme A amount \\(= P\\left(1 + \\frac{15 \\times 4}{100}\\right) = 1.6P\\)<br>Scheme B amount \\(= (P + 1680)\\left(1 + \\frac{25}{100}\\right)^2 = 1.5625(P + 1680)\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1.6P}{1.5625(P + 1680)} = \\frac{4}{5} \\Rightarrow 8P = 6.25(P + 1680)\\)<br>\\(1.75P = 10{,}500 \\Rightarrow P = \\boxed{6000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹6,000.</b>","hi":"योजना A की राशि \\(= P\\left(1 + \\frac{15 \\times 4}{100}\\right) = 1.6P\\)<br>योजना B की राशि \\(= (P + 1680)\\left(1 + \\frac{25}{100}\\right)^2 = 1.5625(P + 1680)\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1.6P}{1.5625(P + 1680)} = \\frac{4}{5} \\Rightarrow 8P = 6.25(P + 1680)\\)<br>\\(1.75P = 10{,}500 \\Rightarrow P = \\boxed{6000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹6,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072754","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"The monthly incomes of A, B and C are in the ratio 4 : 9 : 11, while their expenditures are in the ratio 5 : 7 : 8. A earns ₹32,000 and saves ₹12,000. What is the combined monthly saving of B and C? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A, B और C की मासिक आय 4 : 9 : 11 के अनुपात में है, जबकि उनके व्यय 5 : 7 : 8 के अनुपात में हैं। A ₹32,000 कमाता है और ₹12,000 बचाता है। B और C की संयुक्त मासिक बचत क्या है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹1,00,000"},"2":{"en":"₹96,000"},"3":{"en":"₹98,000"},"4":{"en":"₹1,02,000"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Income unit \\(= \\frac{32{,}000}{4} = 8000\\), so B earns 72,000 and C earns 88,000<br>A's expenditure \\(= 32{,}000 - 12{,}000 = 20{,}000\\); expenditure unit \\(= \\frac{20{,}000}{5} = 4000\\)<br>B's expenditure \\(= 28{,}000\\), C's expenditure \\(= 32{,}000\\)<br>Savings of B and C \\(= (72{,}000 - 28{,}000) + (88{,}000 - 32{,}000) = 44{,}000 + 56{,}000\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1{,}00{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹1,00,000.</b>","hi":"आय इकाई \\(= \\frac{32{,}000}{4} = 8000\\), अतः B की आय 72,000 और C की आय 88,000<br>A का व्यय \\(= 32{,}000 - 12{,}000 = 20{,}000\\); व्यय इकाई \\(= \\frac{20{,}000}{5} = 4000\\)<br>B का व्यय \\(= 28{,}000\\), C का व्यय \\(= 32{,}000\\)<br>B और C की बचत \\(= (72{,}000 - 28{,}000) + (88{,}000 - 32{,}000) = 44{,}000 + 56{,}000\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1{,}00{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹1,00,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072755","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"Person A borrows ₹18,000 at \\(13\\frac{1}{3}\\%\\) per annum simple interest and person B borrows ₹24,000 at \\(8\\frac{1}{3}\\%\\) per annum simple interest on the same date. At the instant when their payable amounts become equal, what is the total simple interest payable by A and B together? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यक्ति A उसी तिथि पर \\(13\\frac{1}{3}\\%\\) प्रति वर्ष साधारण ब्याज पर ₹18,000 उधार लेता है और व्यक्ति B \\(8\\frac{1}{3}\\%\\) प्रति वर्ष साधारण ब्याज पर ₹24,000 उधार लेता है। जिस क्षण उनकी देय राशियाँ बराबर हो जाती हैं, A और B द्वारा मिलाकर देय कुल साधारण ब्याज कितना है? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹60,000"},"2":{"en":"₹62,000"},"3":{"en":"₹64,000"},"4":{"en":"₹66,000"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Interest of A per year \\(= 18{,}000 \\times \\frac{40}{300} = 2400\\)<br>Interest of B per year \\(= 24{,}000 \\times \\frac{25}{300} = 2000\\)<br>Equal payable amounts: \\(18{,}000 + 2400t = 24{,}000 + 2000t \\Rightarrow 400t = 6000 \\Rightarrow t = 15\\) years<br>Total interest \\(= 15(2400 + 2000) = 15 \\times 4400\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{66000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹66,000.</b>","hi":"A का प्रति वर्ष ब्याज \\(= 18{,}000 \\times \\frac{40}{300} = 2400\\)<br>B का प्रति वर्ष ब्याज \\(= 24{,}000 \\times \\frac{25}{300} = 2000\\)<br>देय राशियाँ बराबर: \\(18{,}000 + 2400t = 24{,}000 + 2000t \\Rightarrow 400t = 6000 \\Rightarrow t = 15\\) वर्ष<br>कुल ब्याज \\(= 15(2400 + 2000) = 15 \\times 4400\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{66000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹66,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072756","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) basic banking habits<br>B) financial literacy camps<br>C) promote awareness of<br>D) in rural areas [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B-C-A-D"},"2":{"en":"C-A-D-B"},"3":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"4":{"en":"D-B-C-A"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: B-C-A-D</b><br>B supplies the subject: financial literacy camps.<br>C and A state that they promote awareness of basic banking habits.<br>D identifies the rural setting.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): B-C-A-D.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072757","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Identify the option that best corrects the highlighted part of the sentence for proper grammar and usage.<br>The police <b>is investigating</b> the case thoroughly. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"are investigate"},"2":{"en":"is investigated"},"3":{"en":"are investigating"},"4":{"en":"is to investigate"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Police” is a plural collective noun and takes “are.”</b><br>Correct sentence: “The police <b>are investigating</b> the case thoroughly.”<br>The present continuous describes the ongoing investigation.<br>The other options use incorrect agreement or passive structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): are investigating.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072758","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"What is the one-word substitute for:<br>“An obscure or deliberately evasive statement used to mislead.” [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Non sequitur"},"2":{"en":"Euphemism"},"3":{"en":"Equivocation"},"4":{"en":"Tautology"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Equivocation (अस्पष्ट वचन) = deliberately ambiguous language used to evade.</b><br><b>Non sequitur</b> = conclusion that does not follow logically<br><b>Euphemism</b> = mild expression replacing a blunt one<br><b>Tautology</b> = redundant repetition of meaning<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Equivocation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072759","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"There are four jumbled sentences given below. Your task is to rearrange them into a logically coherent and meaningful paragraph and choose the correct sequence from the given options.<br>1. Several studies show increased enrolment due to this scheme.<br>2. It also incentivises attendance in government schools.<br>3. However, hygiene in food preparation needs stricter monitoring.<br>4. The midday meal scheme aims to improve nutrition among schoolchildren. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-1-2-4"},"2":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"3":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"4":{"en":"4-2-1-3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-2-1-3</b><br>Sentence 4 introduces the scheme’s nutritional aim.<br>Sentence 2 adds attendance, and sentence 1 gives evidence of increased enrolment.<br>Sentence 3 concludes with the hygiene concern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4-2-1-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072760","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"What is the antonym of the word “intrepid”? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Fearless"},"2":{"en":"Humble"},"3":{"en":"Timid"},"4":{"en":"Clear"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Intrepid (निर्भय) = fearless and adventurous.</b><br><b>Fearless (निर्भय)</b> = unafraid<br><b>Humble (विनम्र)</b> = modest<br><b>Timid (डरपोक)</b> = fearful ✔<br><b>Clear (स्पष्ट)</b> = obvious.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Timid.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072761","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Cut the Gordian knot” [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Take a complicated approach"},"2":{"en":"Solve a complex problem decisively"},"3":{"en":"Create confusion intentionally"},"4":{"en":"Tie a knot tightly"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Cut the Gordian knot (कठिन समस्या का सीधा समाधान करना) = solve boldly.</b><br>Example: “The new law cut the Gordian knot of bureaucratic delays.”<br>It favours decisive simplicity, not complication or confusion.<br>The literal knot is not the figurative meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Solve a complex problem decisively.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072762","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Feather in one’s cap” [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Heavy burden"},"2":{"en":"Past failure"},"3":{"en":"Achievement or honor"},"4":{"en":"Strange habit"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>A feather in one’s cap (सम्मान का विषय) = a noteworthy achievement.</b><br>Example: “The award was another feather in her cap.”<br>Burdens, failures and habits are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Achievement or honor.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072763","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"What is the synonym of the word “proponent”? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Critic"},"2":{"en":"Detractor"},"3":{"en":"Opponent"},"4":{"en":"Supporter"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Proponent (समर्थक) = a person advocating something.</b><br><b>Critic (आलोचक)</b> = one who finds fault<br><b>Detractor (निंदक)</b> = disparager<br><b>Opponent (विरोधी)</b> = adversary<br><b>Supporter (समर्थक)</b> = advocate ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Supporter.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072764","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The team decided to ___ the outdated policy and draft a more inclusive one. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"do with"},"2":{"en":"do away with"},"3":{"en":"do about"},"4":{"en":"do off with"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Do away with (समाप्त करना) = abolish.</b><br>The team abolished the outdated policy before drafting a replacement.<br>“Do with” concerns needing or tolerating; “do about” needs a problem object.<br>“Do off with” is not a standard phrasal verb.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): do away with.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072765","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The report's language, laden with technical jargon, served more to ___ than to inform the general public. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"illuminate"},"2":{"en":"obfuscate"},"3":{"en":"clarify"},"4":{"en":"communicate"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Obfuscate (अस्पष्ट करना) = make unclear.</b><br>Jargon obscured rather than informed the general public.<br>Illuminate and clarify mean make clear.<br>Communicate is too general and lacks the intended contrast.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): obfuscate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072766","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>The director looked at the audience and smiled <b>confide</b>. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"confident"},"2":{"en":"confiding"},"3":{"en":"confidently"},"4":{"en":"confidence"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The verb “smiled” requires the adverb “confidently.”</b><br>Correct sentence: “The director … smiled <b>confidently</b>.”<br>“Confident” is an adjective, “confiding” a participle, and “confidence” a noun.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): confidently.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072767","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. All drawings are submitted to the design review committee.<br>2. Clients finalize the space utilization plan.<br>3. The architect prepares preliminary layout drawings.<br>4. Suggestions are incorporated before final approval. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"3":{"en":"3-2-4-1"},"4":{"en":"2-3-1-4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-3-1-4</b><br>Clients finalize the plan, and the architect prepares drawings.<br>The drawings go to the review committee.<br>Suggestions are incorporated before final approval.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2-3-1-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072768","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In today's corporate environment, dysfunctional behavior—taken in the form of manipulation, exclusion, harassment, or passive aggression—is a pervasive undertone. Typically hidden behind professional demeanour or performance targets, such behavior erodes organizational trust and destroys psychological safety. It does not necessarily start from open hostility; instead, it is often system-based—rooted in workplace hierarchies, incentive schemes, and tacit cultural norms.<br><br>Evidence demonstrates that organizations plagued by toxic dynamics experience higher attrition rates, lower employee participation, and higher mental illness. In contrast to conventional management presumptions, productivity is not enhanced by pressure or fear; instead, productivity quietly declines as workers disengage, do a poor job, or abandon work altogether. Toxic cultures also stifle innovation, as fear of retaliation deters dissension and exploration—both essential in competitive markets.<br><br>Leaders tend to misread short-term deliverables as long-term effectiveness, failing to notice that constant exposure to toxicity undermines an organization's strength and overall efficacy. Exacerbating the situation is the tendency to heroize “difficult geniuses”—individual workers who excel on their own but undermine team morale. This glamorization creates a vicious cycle where toxicity is overlooked if it is combined with profitability.<br><br>Abating such conduct is beyond the reach of compliance training or loose ethical guidelines. It necessitates structural change, open accountability, and a culture shift that emphasizes shared well-being as well as monetary profit. Without these, the corporate poison will still disguise itself as greatness, leaving a trail of burnout, turnover, and reduced institutional integrity. “generate 10 hard mcq on this passage with solution and description”.<br><br><br>According to the passage, how does toxic behavior primarily manifest in modern corporate settings? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Through obvious rule-breaking"},"2":{"en":"Through casual office jokes"},"3":{"en":"Through hidden patterns and performance pressure"},"4":{"en":"Through legal misconduct"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Dysfunction hides behind professional demeanour and performance targets.</b><br>Manipulation, exclusion and passive aggression operate as concealed patterns.<br>It need not begin as open hostility or obvious misconduct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Through hidden patterns and performance pressure.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072769","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In today's corporate environment, dysfunctional behavior—taken in the form of manipulation, exclusion, harassment, or passive aggression—is a pervasive undertone. Typically hidden behind professional demeanour or performance targets, such behavior erodes organizational trust and destroys psychological safety. It does not necessarily start from open hostility; instead, it is often system-based—rooted in workplace hierarchies, incentive schemes, and tacit cultural norms.<br><br>Evidence demonstrates that organizations plagued by toxic dynamics experience higher attrition rates, lower employee participation, and higher mental illness. In contrast to conventional management presumptions, productivity is not enhanced by pressure or fear; instead, productivity quietly declines as workers disengage, do a poor job, or abandon work altogether. Toxic cultures also stifle innovation, as fear of retaliation deters dissension and exploration—both essential in competitive markets.<br><br>Leaders tend to misread short-term deliverables as long-term effectiveness, failing to notice that constant exposure to toxicity undermines an organization's strength and overall efficacy. Exacerbating the situation is the tendency to heroize “difficult geniuses”—individual workers who excel on their own but undermine team morale. This glamorization creates a vicious cycle where toxicity is overlooked if it is combined with profitability.<br><br>Abating such conduct is beyond the reach of compliance training or loose ethical guidelines. It necessitates structural change, open accountability, and a culture shift that emphasizes shared well-being as well as monetary profit. Without these, the corporate poison will still disguise itself as greatness, leaving a trail of burnout, turnover, and reduced institutional integrity. “generate 10 hard mcq on this passage with solution and description”.<br><br><br>How does the author suggest toxic behavior is institutionally maintained? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Deficient dialogue structures"},"2":{"en":"Interpersonal frictions"},"3":{"en":"Systemic normalization and incentives"},"4":{"en":"Exogenous economic constraints"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Toxicity is rooted in hierarchies, incentive schemes and tacit norms.</b><br>These institutional systems normalize and sustain the behaviour.<br>The passage does not locate its primary cause in personal friction or external constraints.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Systemic normalization and incentives.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072770","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In today's corporate environment, dysfunctional behavior—taken in the form of manipulation, exclusion, harassment, or passive aggression—is a pervasive undertone. Typically hidden behind professional demeanour or performance targets, such behavior erodes organizational trust and destroys psychological safety. It does not necessarily start from open hostility; instead, it is often system-based—rooted in workplace hierarchies, incentive schemes, and tacit cultural norms.<br><br>Evidence demonstrates that organizations plagued by toxic dynamics experience higher attrition rates, lower employee participation, and higher mental illness. In contrast to conventional management presumptions, productivity is not enhanced by pressure or fear; instead, productivity quietly declines as workers disengage, do a poor job, or abandon work altogether. Toxic cultures also stifle innovation, as fear of retaliation deters dissension and exploration—both essential in competitive markets.<br><br>Leaders tend to misread short-term deliverables as long-term effectiveness, failing to notice that constant exposure to toxicity undermines an organization's strength and overall efficacy. Exacerbating the situation is the tendency to heroize “difficult geniuses”—individual workers who excel on their own but undermine team morale. This glamorization creates a vicious cycle where toxicity is overlooked if it is combined with profitability.<br><br>Abating such conduct is beyond the reach of compliance training or loose ethical guidelines. It necessitates structural change, open accountability, and a culture shift that emphasizes shared well-being as well as monetary profit. Without these, the corporate poison will still disguise itself as greatness, leaving a trail of burnout, turnover, and reduced institutional integrity. “generate 10 hard mcq on this passage with solution and description”.<br><br><br>What is the vicious cycle referred to in the passage? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Targets erode output quality"},"2":{"en":"Strikes disrupt workflow"},"3":{"en":"Praising toxicity sustains dysfunction"},"4":{"en":"Ranks enhance team efficiency"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: “Difficult geniuses” are glamorized, so profitable toxicity is overlooked.</b><br>Praising such individuals allows their damaging conduct to continue.<br>This reinforcement is the vicious cycle.<br>Strikes and ranks are not discussed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Praising toxicity sustains dysfunction.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072771","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In today's corporate environment, dysfunctional behavior—taken in the form of manipulation, exclusion, harassment, or passive aggression—is a pervasive undertone. Typically hidden behind professional demeanour or performance targets, such behavior erodes organizational trust and destroys psychological safety. It does not necessarily start from open hostility; instead, it is often system-based—rooted in workplace hierarchies, incentive schemes, and tacit cultural norms.<br><br>Evidence demonstrates that organizations plagued by toxic dynamics experience higher attrition rates, lower employee participation, and higher mental illness. In contrast to conventional management presumptions, productivity is not enhanced by pressure or fear; instead, productivity quietly declines as workers disengage, do a poor job, or abandon work altogether. Toxic cultures also stifle innovation, as fear of retaliation deters dissension and exploration—both essential in competitive markets.<br><br>Leaders tend to misread short-term deliverables as long-term effectiveness, failing to notice that constant exposure to toxicity undermines an organization's strength and overall efficacy. Exacerbating the situation is the tendency to heroize “difficult geniuses”—individual workers who excel on their own but undermine team morale. This glamorization creates a vicious cycle where toxicity is overlooked if it is combined with profitability.<br><br>Abating such conduct is beyond the reach of compliance training or loose ethical guidelines. It necessitates structural change, open accountability, and a culture shift that emphasizes shared well-being as well as monetary profit. Without these, the corporate poison will still disguise itself as greatness, leaving a trail of burnout, turnover, and reduced institutional integrity. “generate 10 hard mcq on this passage with solution and description”.<br><br><br>What can be inferred about “psychological safety” in the workplace? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It depends solely on job security"},"2":{"en":"It increases through stricter regulation"},"3":{"en":"It is eroded by manipulation and passive aggression"},"4":{"en":"It thrives under pressure"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Manipulation, harassment and passive aggression destroy psychological safety.</b><br>Toxic conduct erodes the trust employees need to participate openly.<br>It does not thrive under fear or pressure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): It is eroded by manipulation and passive aggression.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072772","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In today's corporate environment, dysfunctional behavior—taken in the form of manipulation, exclusion, harassment, or passive aggression—is a pervasive undertone. Typically hidden behind professional demeanour or performance targets, such behavior erodes organizational trust and destroys psychological safety. It does not necessarily start from open hostility; instead, it is often system-based—rooted in workplace hierarchies, incentive schemes, and tacit cultural norms.<br><br>Evidence demonstrates that organizations plagued by toxic dynamics experience higher attrition rates, lower employee participation, and higher mental illness. In contrast to conventional management presumptions, productivity is not enhanced by pressure or fear; instead, productivity quietly declines as workers disengage, do a poor job, or abandon work altogether. Toxic cultures also stifle innovation, as fear of retaliation deters dissension and exploration—both essential in competitive markets.<br><br>Leaders tend to misread short-term deliverables as long-term effectiveness, failing to notice that constant exposure to toxicity undermines an organization's strength and overall efficacy. Exacerbating the situation is the tendency to heroize “difficult geniuses”—individual workers who excel on their own but undermine team morale. This glamorization creates a vicious cycle where toxicity is overlooked if it is combined with profitability.<br><br>Abating such conduct is beyond the reach of compliance training or loose ethical guidelines. It necessitates structural change, open accountability, and a culture shift that emphasizes shared well-being as well as monetary profit. Without these, the corporate poison will still disguise itself as greatness, leaving a trail of burnout, turnover, and reduced institutional integrity. “generate 10 hard mcq on this passage with solution and description”.<br><br><br>What is the author's critique of standard leadership evaluation practices? [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Overweighting of short-term deliverables"},"2":{"en":"Dependence on employee self-assessment"},"3":{"en":"Emphasis on procedural uniformity"},"4":{"en":"Undervaluing symbolic leadership"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Leaders mistake short-term deliverables for long-term effectiveness.</b><br>This overemphasis hides the institutional damage caused by persistent toxicity.<br>Self-assessment, uniformity and symbolic leadership are not the critique.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Overweighting of short-term deliverables.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072773","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>The evidence is believed to have been tampered with by unknown individuals. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Unknown individuals believed to have tampered with the evidence."},"2":{"en":"Unknown individuals have been believed to have tampered with the evidence."},"3":{"en":"Unknown individuals are believed to have tampered with the evidence."},"4":{"en":"Unknown individuals are believed to will have tampered with the evidence."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Object + is believed + to have been + V3 + by agent” becomes “Agent + is/are believed + to have + V3 + object”.</b><br>The agent “unknown individuals” becomes the subject; “is believed” changes to the plural “are believed”, and “to have been tampered with” becomes “to have tampered with”.<br>Active: Unknown individuals are believed to have tampered with the evidence.<br>Option 1 drops “are”, option 2 wrongly uses “have been believed”, and option 4 “to will have” is ungrammatical.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Unknown individuals are believed to have tampered with the evidence.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072774","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>IMPECUNIOUS</b> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Poor"},"2":{"en":"Affluent"},"3":{"en":"Wealthy"},"4":{"en":"Rich"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Impecunious (निर्धन) = having little or no money.</b><br><b>Poor (गरीब)</b> = lacking money ✔<br><b>Affluent (धनी)</b> = wealthy<br><b>Wealthy (संपन्न)</b> = rich; <b>rich (अमीर)</b> = affluent; synonyms: penniless, indigent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Poor.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072775","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Succinct</b> [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Verbose"},"2":{"en":"Concise"},"3":{"en":"Terse"},"4":{"en":"Brief"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Succinct (संक्षिप्त) = briefly and clearly expressed.</b><br><b>Verbose (शब्दाडंबरपूर्ण)</b> = using too many words ✔<br><b>Concise (संक्षिप्त)</b> = brief<br><b>Terse (संक्षिप्त)</b> = brief; <b>brief (अल्प)</b> = short.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Verbose.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072776","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a term meaning “study of existence”. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ontollogy"},"2":{"en":"Ontologie"},"3":{"en":"Ontology"},"4":{"en":"Ontolegy"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Ontology (अस्तित्व-विज्ञान) = the philosophical study of being.</b><br>The correct spelling is “ontology.”<br><b>Ontollogy</b> doubles “l”; <b>ontologie</b> uses final “ie.”<br><b>Ontolegy</b> omits “o.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Ontology.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072777","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A word that is no longer in use”. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jargon"},"2":{"en":"Colloquialism"},"3":{"en":"Archaism"},"4":{"en":"Neologism"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Archaism (प्राचीन शब्द) = an obsolete word or expression.</b><br><b>Jargon</b> = specialized terminology<br><b>Colloquialism</b> = informal expression<br><b>Neologism</b> = newly coined word<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Archaism.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072778","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Egregious"},"2":{"en":"Inimitible"},"3":{"en":"Garrulous"},"4":{"en":"Pugnacious"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Inimitable (अनूठा) = impossible to imitate.</b><br><b>Inimitible</b> incorrectly uses “i” in the suffix; use “-able.”<br><b>Egregious</b> = conspicuously bad.<br><b>Garrulous</b> = talkative; <b>pugnacious</b> = combative.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Inimitible.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072779","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of the study of fingerprints. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dermatoglyphic"},"2":{"en":"Dermatoglyphics"},"3":{"en":"Dermatoglyphiks"},"4":{"en":"Dermatoglyfics"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Dermatoglyphics (त्वचा-रेखा-विज्ञान) = the study of skin ridge patterns.</b><br>The correct spelling is “dermatoglyphics.”<br><b>Dermatoglyphic</b> is the singular adjective rather than the study.<br>The other options use “k” or “f” incorrectly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Dermatoglyphics.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072780","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The mystic interpreted the <b>oracle’s</b> message symbolically. [SSC CGL 27/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Oracle database crashed during the migration."},"2":{"en":"The villagers consulted the oracle every full moon."},"3":{"en":"The oracle’s cave is still a sacred site."},"4":{"en":"Her verses echoed the oracle’s cryptic tone."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Oracle = a prophetic source, or Oracle = a database software product.</b><br>The original uses the prophetic meaning.<br>Option A uses the proper name of the database system.<br>The other options retain the mystical meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The Oracle database crashed during the migration.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};